1
00:00:53,262 --> 00:00:55,306
<i>[ Man Narrating]
This is the Earth at a time</i>

2
00:00:55,389 --> 00:00:59,644
<i>when the dinosaurs roamed
a lush and fertile planet.</i>

3
00:01:07,526 --> 00:01:11,113
<i>A piece of rock just six miles wide</i>

4
00:01:11,197 --> 00:01:13,157
<i>changed all that.</i>

5
00:01:21,082 --> 00:01:25,002
<i>It hit with the force
of 10,000 nuclear weapons.</i>

6
00:01:28,047 --> 00:01:32,718
<i>A trillion tons of dirt and rock
hurtled into the atmosphere,</i>

7
00:01:32,802 --> 00:01:35,513
<i>creating a suffocating blanket of dust</i>

8
00:01:35,596 --> 00:01:38,182
<i>the sun was powerless to penetrate</i>

9
00:01:38,266 --> 00:01:40,309
<i>for a thousand years.</i>

10
00:01:48,818 --> 00:01:50,736
<i>It happened before.</i>

11
00:01:51,988 --> 00:01:53,948
<i>It will happen again.</i>

12
00:01:55,700 --> 00:01:58,411
<i>It's just a question of when.</i>

13
00:02:14,385 --> 00:02:16,345
<i>[ Man Chattering]</i>

14
00:02:19,265 --> 00:02:21,225
<i>[ Man ] Houston, affirmative.</i>

15
00:02:23,144 --> 00:02:24,520
<i>Now try again.</i>

16
00:02:24,603 --> 00:02:27,648
<i>[ Man On Radio Chattering]</i>

17
00:02:28,190 --> 00:02:29,817
<i>Almost got it.</i>

18
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:31,152
<i>[ Grunts]</i>

19
00:02:33,029 --> 00:02:36,741
<i>- Atlantis, I'm almost there.</i>
- Houston, Pete's lookin' real strong.

20
00:02:36,824 --> 00:02:40,077
Okay, Pete, we got that coupling
on the board here now.

21
00:02:40,161 --> 00:02:43,497
We'll give you the go-ahead
from down here when it's in alignment.

22
00:02:43,581 --> 00:02:46,292
Sounds good. Give me ten seconds.

23
00:02:47,418 --> 00:02:48,586
[ Sighs ]

24
00:02:48,669 --> 00:02:51,088
His heart rate's racing. Hey, Pete.

25
00:02:51,172 --> 00:02:52,673
- It's Truman.
<i>- Hey.</i>

26
00:02:52,757 --> 00:02:54,884
- How you doing up there, hoss?
<i>- Pretty good.</i>

27
00:02:54,967 --> 00:02:57,345
Listen, Pete, we got an eye
on your meds here.

28
00:02:57,428 --> 00:02:58,679
I'll give you a buffalo nickel

29
00:02:58,763 --> 00:03:00,681
if you'll calm down just a little bit.

30
00:03:00,765 --> 00:03:03,476
<i>- Can you do that for me?</i>
-Whatever you say.

31
00:03:03,559 --> 00:03:07,063
Okay, now, we got plenty of time,
buddy, so don't you worry.

32
00:03:11,192 --> 00:03:13,361
Looking good here.

33
00:03:13,444 --> 00:03:14,487
He'll be all right.

34
00:03:14,570 --> 00:03:16,614
<i>- Go ahead,</i> Atlantis.
<i>- Roger that, Houston.</i>

35
00:03:16,697 --> 00:03:18,449
Suggest we start reeling Pete in.

36
00:03:29,919 --> 00:03:31,379
<i>[Buzzing]</i>

37
00:03:31,462 --> 00:03:33,422
- What the hell is that?
- My Lord.

38
00:03:36,384 --> 00:03:38,803
[ Screaming ]

39
00:03:39,804 --> 00:03:40,846
<i>We're down!</i>

40
00:03:43,808 --> 00:03:45,601
<i>Houston!</i>

41
00:03:48,020 --> 00:03:50,564
We've lost all contact.

42
00:03:52,650 --> 00:03:54,860
Stewart, play that tape back!

43
00:03:58,489 --> 00:04:01,325
<i>[ Screaming] Houston!</i>

44
00:04:04,120 --> 00:04:05,746
Multiple bogies! Multiple bogies!

45
00:04:05,830 --> 00:04:08,916
Sector five, niner. I have three. Now five.

46
00:04:08,999 --> 00:04:11,043
- Unidentified tracks.
- My screen's full.

47
00:04:11,127 --> 00:04:13,170
Multiple tracks headed toward
the Atlantic seaboard!

48
00:04:13,254 --> 00:04:14,839
This could be a surprise missile attack.

49
00:04:14,922 --> 00:04:18,008
[ Alarm Blaring ]

50
00:04:20,678 --> 00:04:23,931
Mr. President, the shuttle
<i>Atlantis</i> just exploded in space.

51
00:04:24,014 --> 00:04:28,060
Okay, I want three groups!
One, internal malfunction.

52
00:04:28,144 --> 00:04:30,980
Get the log tape.
Start working back. Maybe it's a glitch.

53
00:04:31,063 --> 00:04:33,941
Two, I want NORAD,
Space Command and the 50th tactical,

54
00:04:34,024 --> 00:04:36,444
comparing all the space junk
you tracked in every orbit.

55
00:04:36,527 --> 00:04:38,988
I want you to check, recheck
and then do it all over again.

56
00:04:39,071 --> 00:04:41,991
Number three, wild cards.
Anything and everything.

57
00:04:42,074 --> 00:04:45,578
All right? Now, Big Ross, get on
the telephone. Wake up 11,000 people.

58
00:04:45,661 --> 00:04:47,121
- Walt, get 'em going.
- Let's go!

59
00:04:47,204 --> 00:04:52,042
Karl. Karl! Karl.

60
00:04:54,086 --> 00:04:56,964
Karl! Your Stouffer's pot pie's

61
00:04:57,047 --> 00:04:59,633
been on the table almost ten hours.

62
00:04:59,717 --> 00:05:02,011
- I want a divorce.
- Dottie, I'm on to something big here.

63
00:05:02,094 --> 00:05:05,431
I... I don't know what this is, but it
looks like something's burnin' up there.

64
00:05:05,514 --> 00:05:07,349
Go get my phone book, will you?
Get my phone book.

65
00:05:07,433 --> 00:05:09,351
Get those names
of those guys from NASA.

66
00:05:09,435 --> 00:05:14,398
Excuse me! Am I wearing a sign
that says, "Karl's Slave"?

67
00:05:14,482 --> 00:05:17,651
Go get my goddamn phone book!

68
00:05:17,735 --> 00:05:20,946
Get the book! Get the book!
Get the book!

69
00:05:25,576 --> 00:05:29,163
Space Command is reporting negative.
That is zero global launches.

70
00:05:29,246 --> 00:05:31,499
It might just be a piece of the shuttle
breaking up as it comes in.

71
00:05:31,582 --> 00:05:32,791
It might be Santa Claus.

72
00:05:32,875 --> 00:05:36,128
Until we get definitive,
reliable confirmation, General,

73
00:05:36,212 --> 00:05:38,380
we go to DEFCON Three.

74
00:05:43,511 --> 00:05:47,139
<i>I'm gettin' ready for the big time</i>

75
00:05:47,223 --> 00:05:50,935
<i>Someday you're gonna say
I'm big time, too</i>

76
00:05:51,936 --> 00:05:54,021
Hey, little man! Little Richard!

77
00:05:54,104 --> 00:05:56,690
Me and you, man!
We're going to the top, baby!

78
00:05:56,774 --> 00:06:00,778
Big time! I ain't gonna be ridin'
this bike for the rest of my life.

79
00:06:00,861 --> 00:06:03,239
You know what I'm sayin'?
I'm gettin' a motorcycle, baby.

80
00:06:03,322 --> 00:06:05,449
We're gonna travel in style.

81
00:06:06,450 --> 00:06:10,287
<i>I'm gettin' ready for the big time</i>

82
00:06:10,371 --> 00:06:12,873
<i>Someday I'm gonna be in big time news</i>

83
00:06:12,957 --> 00:06:16,877
Watch where you're goin'. I bet you,
none of you all stop for brothers.

84
00:06:16,961 --> 00:06:18,629
Slow down, Little Richard.

85
00:06:18,712 --> 00:06:20,923
You've been ridin' all morning.
You gotta take a dump?

86
00:06:23,384 --> 00:06:25,135
<i>We interrupt our regularly
scheduled programme...</i>

87
00:06:25,219 --> 00:06:26,554
- What happened?
- <i>...to bring you this special report.</i>

88
00:06:26,637 --> 00:06:27,680
Shh, shh, shh.

89
00:06:27,763 --> 00:06:32,309
<i>The shuttle</i> Atlantis <i>exploded in space
at 3:47 a.m., Eastern Standard Time.</i>

90
00:06:32,393 --> 00:06:34,853
[ Growling ]

91
00:06:34,937 --> 00:06:36,188
[ Squeaking ]

92
00:06:36,272 --> 00:06:38,524
Hey! Get, get.

93
00:06:38,607 --> 00:06:41,527
[ Chattering ]

94
00:06:41,610 --> 00:06:44,321
- That's my Godzilla. Come on, now.
- Yo, fool!

95
00:06:44,405 --> 00:06:46,574
Don't be kickin' Little Richard.
What the hell your problem?

96
00:06:46,657 --> 00:06:49,910
That dog's eatin' my Godzilla. What's
a little runt like you gonna do about it?

97
00:06:49,994 --> 00:06:52,079
Get him, Richard. Sic him.
If I wasn't no Christian,

98
00:06:52,162 --> 00:06:56,125
I'd be throwin' your fat pineapple-eatin'
ass through the window.

99
00:06:59,545 --> 00:07:02,506
[ Screaming ]

100
00:07:08,429 --> 00:07:09,513
Why we not going?

101
00:07:09,597 --> 00:07:11,599
You know why?
'Cause this is New York City.

102
00:07:11,682 --> 00:07:14,977
Anything could happen. Let's see.
Could've been a terrorist bomb.

103
00:07:15,060 --> 00:07:18,439
Could've been a dead body. Somebody
shot, stabbed, and it's Friday, payday.

104
00:07:18,522 --> 00:07:20,608
Dude, somebody probably didn't
get their paycheck. Yes?

105
00:07:20,691 --> 00:07:22,151
I want to go shopping.

106
00:07:22,234 --> 00:07:26,655
Me, too, but we ain't goin' nowhere
'cause this is a traffic jam.

107
00:07:27,364 --> 00:07:28,824
- Little Richard!
- Right over there!

108
00:07:28,907 --> 00:07:29,992
[ Screaming ]

109
00:07:30,075 --> 00:07:31,994
Little Richard!

110
00:07:32,077 --> 00:07:33,954
Hang on, Little Richard. I'm comin'!

111
00:07:34,038 --> 00:07:35,623
[ Whimpering ]

112
00:07:35,706 --> 00:07:38,417
Don't you worry about it.
I'm gonna get you outta there!

113
00:07:38,500 --> 00:07:41,545
You okay, buddy?
Don't worry about it. Hang in there.

114
00:07:42,379 --> 00:07:44,632
Somebody dial 911!

115
00:07:44,715 --> 00:07:46,675
My screen's full.
They're all over the place.

116
00:07:46,759 --> 00:07:48,135
Bogies are breachin' the atmosphere

117
00:07:48,218 --> 00:07:50,346
from Finland down
the North American seaboard.

118
00:07:53,932 --> 00:07:56,268
[ Screaming ]

119
00:08:01,190 --> 00:08:02,900
Whoa!

120
00:08:05,986 --> 00:08:07,446
Look at that!

121
00:08:13,661 --> 00:08:15,788
Oh, we at war!

122
00:08:15,871 --> 00:08:17,706
[ Screaming Continues ]

123
00:08:18,165 --> 00:08:19,750
Saddam Hussein is bombing us!

124
00:08:48,487 --> 00:08:50,698
[ Man Screaming ]

125
00:09:14,972 --> 00:09:16,014
Let's stay focused. We need to

126
00:09:16,098 --> 00:09:18,058
- map the trajectory now.
- That could take a week.

127
00:09:18,142 --> 00:09:20,644
Just find it, okay? I wanna know if
the worst is over or if it's on its way.

128
00:09:20,728 --> 00:09:22,438
We've got General Kimsey on the line.

129
00:09:22,521 --> 00:09:25,399
We've got hits from Finland
to South Carolina.

130
00:09:25,482 --> 00:09:27,151
We know they're not missiles.
Now what the hell is it?

131
00:09:27,234 --> 00:09:30,654
It's a meteor shower.
That's what took out the shuttle.

132
00:09:30,821 --> 00:09:33,490
[ Overlapping Chattering ]

133
00:09:33,782 --> 00:09:36,118
I've got the president
on <i>Air Force One</i> demanding answers.

134
00:09:36,994 --> 00:09:38,579
<i>[ General] Is it over?</i>

135
00:09:38,662 --> 00:09:42,166
General, we've got 11,000 people at
NASA trying to figure that out right now.

136
00:09:42,249 --> 00:09:43,250
When we know, you'll know.

137
00:09:45,711 --> 00:09:48,005
[ Sirens Wailing ]

138
00:09:48,589 --> 00:09:50,924
Okay, Karl, listen.
I want you to take your time.

139
00:09:51,008 --> 00:09:52,468
Yes, sir. You're definitely the first.

140
00:09:52,551 --> 00:09:57,598
Okay, first coordinate.
One-two-three-nine. 1239, right?

141
00:09:58,599 --> 00:10:01,727
- F.B.I. locked his location.
- Saw an explosion in space.

142
00:10:01,810 --> 00:10:03,270
Okay.

143
00:10:03,353 --> 00:10:04,521
[ Whispering ]

144
00:10:04,605 --> 00:10:07,191
- Listen, Karl, this is top secret.
- Sir, I'm retired Navy.

145
00:10:07,274 --> 00:10:10,319
I know all about classified.
But one more thing.

146
00:10:10,402 --> 00:10:12,321
The person that finds her
gets to name her, right?

147
00:10:12,404 --> 00:10:16,867
- Yes, that's right.
- I wanna name her Dottie, after my wife.

148
00:10:16,950 --> 00:10:20,788
She's a vicious life-suckin' bitch
from which there's no escape.

149
00:10:20,871 --> 00:10:23,624
- That's sweet, Karl.
- S.D.I., this is flight director!

150
00:10:23,707 --> 00:10:25,417
I wanna get that Hubble movin',
and I want it now.

151
00:10:25,501 --> 00:10:26,877
Roger that.

152
00:10:26,960 --> 00:10:28,212
We're movin' the Hubble!

153
00:10:34,968 --> 00:10:36,261
[ Man ] It's enormous.

154
00:10:36,345 --> 00:10:40,390
This is the anomaly at 1643.

155
00:10:41,809 --> 00:10:45,729
Here is the anomaly at 1658,

156
00:10:45,813 --> 00:10:49,483
<i>and here is the anomaly at 1700.</i>

157
00:10:49,566 --> 00:10:52,486
Enough with this anomaly horseshit!

158
00:10:52,569 --> 00:10:55,489
<i>- What is this thing?</i>
-It's an asteroid, sir.

159
00:10:55,906 --> 00:10:58,325
How big are we talking?

160
00:10:58,408 --> 00:11:00,369
Sir, our best estimate is 97.6 billion...

161
00:11:00,452 --> 00:11:03,455
- It's the size of Texas, Mr. President.
- Y-Yes, sir.

162
00:11:03,539 --> 00:11:05,999
Dan, we didn't see this thing coming?

163
00:11:06,083 --> 00:11:08,293
Well, our object collision
budget's a million dollars.

164
00:11:08,377 --> 00:11:10,504
That allows us to track
about three percent of the sky.

165
00:11:10,587 --> 00:11:12,965
And begging your pardon, sir,
it's a big-ass sky.

166
00:11:13,048 --> 00:11:14,716
- And the ones this morning?
<i>- Those are nothing.</i>

167
00:11:14,800 --> 00:11:16,510
<i>They're the size of basketballs</i>

168
00:11:16,593 --> 00:11:18,345
and Volkswagens, things like that.

169
00:11:18,428 --> 00:11:23,183
<i>- Is this going to hit us?</i>
-We're efforting that as we speak, sir.

170
00:11:23,267 --> 00:11:25,936
- What kind of damage are we...
<i>- Damage?</i>

171
00:11:27,229 --> 00:11:29,398
Total, sir.

172
00:11:29,481 --> 00:11:31,900
It's what we call a global killer.

173
00:11:31,984 --> 00:11:34,194
The end of mankind.

174
00:11:34,278 --> 00:11:36,196
Doesn't matter where it hits.

175
00:11:36,280 --> 00:11:38,866
Nothing would survive.
Not even bacteria.

176
00:11:38,949 --> 00:11:42,661
My God. What do we do?

177
00:11:42,870 --> 00:11:44,788
[ Groaning ]

178
00:11:51,753 --> 00:11:55,007
We have 18 days before it hits Earth.

179
00:12:05,392 --> 00:12:06,560
<i>[ Man ] Have mercy</i>

180
00:12:06,643 --> 00:12:08,228
Rise and shine!

181
00:12:08,312 --> 00:12:10,272
[ Yelling ]

182
00:12:10,355 --> 00:12:13,567
Stop the drilling!
Stop the drilling! Stop the drilling!

183
00:12:13,650 --> 00:12:16,069
Fore!

184
00:12:16,153 --> 00:12:18,071
Stop the drilling! Stop the drilling!

185
00:12:18,155 --> 00:12:21,074
- Hey!
- Hey, that was close!

186
00:12:21,158 --> 00:12:24,077
[ Chuckling ]

187
00:12:24,786 --> 00:12:27,831
I give you 50,000 a year in donations.

188
00:12:27,915 --> 00:12:29,416
What do you think
they're so mad about, Chick?

189
00:12:29,499 --> 00:12:32,377
Well, I think they feel that
drilling for oil is an evil thing.

190
00:12:32,461 --> 00:12:35,297
You know how much diesel
that clunker boat pumps out an hour?

191
00:12:35,380 --> 00:12:40,761
I just found out something interesting.
Number two chewed 180 feet last night.

192
00:12:40,844 --> 00:12:43,263
- Who do we have to thank for this?
- I'll give you two guesses.

193
00:12:43,347 --> 00:12:45,182
But you're only gonna need one.

194
00:12:45,265 --> 00:12:47,517
Goddamn it, A.J.!

195
00:12:47,601 --> 00:12:49,519
A.J.!

196
00:12:51,980 --> 00:12:54,858
A.J.! A.J., you in here?

197
00:12:54,942 --> 00:12:57,653
Oh, that's just perfect. In bed. Get up!

198
00:12:57,736 --> 00:13:01,782
- Uh, hey, you wanted to see me?
- Yeah, I was lookin' for ya.

199
00:13:01,865 --> 00:13:03,617
You're pissed. Okay, I can see that.

200
00:13:03,700 --> 00:13:06,828
No. You know what, A.J.?
I'm not pissed. You've seen me pissed.

201
00:13:06,912 --> 00:13:08,747
This is way, way beyond pissed, though.

202
00:13:08,830 --> 00:13:10,916
You know I shut down
number two last night, right?

203
00:13:10,999 --> 00:13:13,543
- Yeah, man, I had a hunch on that.
- Let me tell you something.

204
00:13:13,627 --> 00:13:16,421
Someday, many years from now,
when you're all growed up,

205
00:13:16,505 --> 00:13:17,839
and you got your own oil company

206
00:13:17,923 --> 00:13:20,801
and $8 million of your own money
on the contract,

207
00:13:20,884 --> 00:13:24,513
you can do whatever comes into that
little A.J.-idiotin' mind of yours you want.

208
00:13:24,596 --> 00:13:26,765
But as long as it says
"Harry Stamper Oil" on the rig,

209
00:13:26,848 --> 00:13:28,141
you will not disobey my rules.

210
00:13:28,225 --> 00:13:30,102
- You got that?
- Yeah, I do got it.

211
00:13:30,185 --> 00:13:32,396
All right, now I need to hear
five words from you.

212
00:13:32,479 --> 00:13:34,690
- Uh...
- I'll...

213
00:13:34,773 --> 00:13:36,817
[ Together ] Never do that again.

214
00:13:36,900 --> 00:13:39,403
I'm a fool. That was idiotic.
I... I mean, that was stupid.

215
00:13:39,486 --> 00:13:41,154
I'm an idiot. I know
what name's on the sign. I'm not...

216
00:13:41,238 --> 00:13:42,990
- What's goin' on here?
- What's goin' on?

217
00:13:43,073 --> 00:13:44,950
Well, I mean, you know,
I screwed up. I'm a little edgy.

218
00:13:45,033 --> 00:13:48,245
- How long you work for me?
- Five wonderful years.

219
00:13:48,328 --> 00:13:51,415
In five years, you have never
apologized to me this quickly.

220
00:13:51,498 --> 00:13:53,500
Something's going on here.
I'm gonna find out what it is.

221
00:13:53,583 --> 00:13:56,294
[ Stammering ]
Well, I'm turning over a new leaf.

222
00:13:56,378 --> 00:13:57,504
I'm trying to learn from the man.

223
00:13:57,587 --> 00:13:59,673
What would Harry do?

224
00:14:05,262 --> 00:14:07,180
I'm at a loss for words.

225
00:14:08,598 --> 00:14:10,017
Okay, I can explain this.

226
00:14:10,100 --> 00:14:11,560
- You can explain that?
- I can.

227
00:14:11,643 --> 00:14:15,272
I would really like an explanation.
You just stay right here.

228
00:14:20,944 --> 00:14:22,863
Grace?

229
00:14:23,405 --> 00:14:24,823
Hi, Harry.

230
00:14:24,906 --> 00:14:28,118
I have asked you repeatedly
to call me Dad.

231
00:14:28,201 --> 00:14:29,578
Sorry, Harry.

232
00:14:29,661 --> 00:14:31,955
Get up and get your clothes on.

233
00:14:34,708 --> 00:14:37,377
You just stay right there.
I'll be right back.

234
00:14:44,468 --> 00:14:47,012
Here's what we're gonna do.
I want every strategy we've got

235
00:14:47,095 --> 00:14:48,388
on near-Earth object collision.

236
00:14:48,472 --> 00:14:50,891
Okay? Any ideas, any programmes,

237
00:14:50,974 --> 00:14:54,019
anything you sketched
on a pizza box or cocktail napkin.

238
00:14:54,102 --> 00:14:56,104
For 30 years,
they questioned the need for NASA.

239
00:14:56,188 --> 00:14:57,314
Today, we're gonna give 'em
the answer.

240
00:15:01,318 --> 00:15:03,361
You know about this, Rockhound?

241
00:15:03,445 --> 00:15:06,156
- You knew?
- No, I had no idea.

242
00:15:07,824 --> 00:15:09,993
Where's Harry?

243
00:15:10,077 --> 00:15:13,330
Harry, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.
I understand, okay?

244
00:15:13,413 --> 00:15:15,665
You're mad.
Who... Who wouldn't be mad?

245
00:15:15,749 --> 00:15:17,751
- He's gonna shoot you.
- Nah, no, he's not.

246
00:15:17,834 --> 00:15:18,877
Oh, shit.

247
00:15:18,960 --> 00:15:21,963
[ Screaming ]

248
00:15:22,047 --> 00:15:25,008
- Harry!
- What's wrong with you?

249
00:15:25,092 --> 00:15:27,094
Make your peace with God, A.J.!

250
00:15:27,177 --> 00:15:29,471
This guy's got a gun, man.
He's shooting at me.

251
00:15:29,554 --> 00:15:31,264
Harry, this is not funny!

252
00:15:31,348 --> 00:15:33,809
Harry, listen to me!
We can talk this over!

253
00:15:33,892 --> 00:15:37,187
- Oh, is this a serious thing?
- Yeah, pretty serious.

254
00:15:37,270 --> 00:15:38,438
- Bear!
- What's up?

255
00:15:38,522 --> 00:15:40,857
He's shootin' at me. You see Harry
comin', crack him with that wrench.

256
00:15:40,941 --> 00:15:44,152
You told A.J.'s dad just before he died
that you would take care of the boy.

257
00:15:44,236 --> 00:15:46,530
Now I'm not sure that
shootin' him is takin' care of him.

258
00:15:46,613 --> 00:15:47,697
Why don't you put the gun down?

259
00:15:47,781 --> 00:15:49,658
You don't want none of this.
Get out of my way.

260
00:15:49,741 --> 00:15:51,952
Just tryin' to give my man
a head start, that's all.

261
00:15:52,035 --> 00:15:53,286
Not to mention the fact that I don't think

262
00:15:53,370 --> 00:15:54,955
you wanna kill
the best man on your crew,

263
00:15:55,038 --> 00:15:57,457
- before we strike oil.
- Aw, Chick, I ain't gonna kill him.

264
00:15:57,541 --> 00:16:00,293
Just gonna take a foot off.
A man can work with one foot.

265
00:16:00,377 --> 00:16:03,296
You remember old Frank Marx who
worked with one hand all them years?

266
00:16:03,380 --> 00:16:04,589
Yeah, but he wasn't very good.

267
00:16:04,673 --> 00:16:07,425
Harry, put the gun down!
You're acting insane!

268
00:16:07,509 --> 00:16:10,053
Now, honey, go get some clothes on
and get out of the way.

269
00:16:10,137 --> 00:16:14,307
- You can't control my life!
- Fine. Clothes. Now!

270
00:16:14,391 --> 00:16:15,559
All right, stop! All right!

271
00:16:15,642 --> 00:16:17,602
It was funny for a minute.
It's not funny any more.

272
00:16:19,521 --> 00:16:22,566
- Fuck!
- Harry, this is illegal, man.

273
00:16:22,649 --> 00:16:24,818
I'm temporarily insane, Rock.
It's all right.

274
00:16:24,901 --> 00:16:27,904
[ Screaming ]

275
00:16:29,906 --> 00:16:31,658
- Do I look like I'm crazy to you?
- Well...

276
00:16:31,741 --> 00:16:33,827
Harry! Hey, just cool down.

277
00:16:33,910 --> 00:16:36,413
What are you doing?
Harry, stop! Cut it out.

278
00:16:36,496 --> 00:16:38,498
- All right, Harry.
- All right, now, listen.

279
00:16:38,582 --> 00:16:42,252
Man to man. I'm serious. I love her.

280
00:16:42,335 --> 00:16:44,254
Way wrong answer!

281
00:16:45,547 --> 00:16:47,007
[ Screaming ]

282
00:16:47,090 --> 00:16:49,843
- Whoa, whoa, Harry. It's gettin' real.
- Harry! Come on, Harry!

283
00:16:49,926 --> 00:16:52,554
- You shot me!
- You shot him.

284
00:16:52,637 --> 00:16:54,514
That bullet never got close.
Just a ricochet.

285
00:16:54,598 --> 00:16:57,058
You know, it's all funny
till somebody gets shot in the leg!

286
00:16:57,142 --> 00:17:01,104
Hey, pucker up.
We got clients incoming.

287
00:17:02,272 --> 00:17:05,525
Uh, b-back in-in... In 1974,

288
00:17:05,609 --> 00:17:07,152
we-we first got the idea

289
00:17:07,235 --> 00:17:09,112
the-the possibility
that-that a meteor or an asteroid...

290
00:17:09,196 --> 00:17:11,948
I need somebody who's had a little less
caffeine this morning. Doc, translate.

291
00:17:12,032 --> 00:17:16,953
Yes, sir. Our first feasibility plan was
to use a spread-focus laser generator

292
00:17:17,037 --> 00:17:18,997
to heat the object
to the point of fracture.

293
00:17:19,080 --> 00:17:21,625
That's like shooting a B.B. gun
at a freight train, Doc.

294
00:17:21,708 --> 00:17:23,335
Uh, some of us have got this idea.

295
00:17:23,418 --> 00:17:26,922
We wanna land a craft,
deploy solar sails.

296
00:17:27,005 --> 00:17:32,636
You'll have a big canopy. Solar winds
will be caught by these Mylar sails.

297
00:17:33,470 --> 00:17:35,555
- Okay...
- Come on, guys!

298
00:17:35,639 --> 00:17:39,309
We gotta come up with something
realistic here. We got 18 days.

299
00:17:39,392 --> 00:17:43,188
That's 431 hours, 15 minutes
and 18 seconds.

300
00:17:43,271 --> 00:17:45,815
Time's a luxury we don't have. What?

301
00:17:48,902 --> 00:17:50,820
Listen, Harry, A.J. is my choice.

302
00:17:50,904 --> 00:17:52,405
My choice and not yours.

303
00:17:52,489 --> 00:17:54,407
He's the only one in
your age bracket, Grace.

304
00:17:54,491 --> 00:17:56,409
It's not a choice. It's a lack of options.

305
00:17:56,493 --> 00:17:58,954
I don't know
what in the world makes you think

306
00:17:59,037 --> 00:18:01,665
that you have the right
to tell me what to do any more, Harry.

307
00:18:01,748 --> 00:18:03,708
I suppose being your father
doesn't count, huh?

308
00:18:03,792 --> 00:18:05,585
- Not really.
- Since when?

309
00:18:05,669 --> 00:18:08,922
Since I reached the age of ten
and became older than you, Harry.

310
00:18:09,005 --> 00:18:11,299
Since Mom split.
Why don't you take your pick?

311
00:18:11,383 --> 00:18:13,927
Look, I understand that
you are handicapped

312
00:18:14,010 --> 00:18:16,721
by natural immaturity, and I forgive you.

313
00:18:16,805 --> 00:18:19,724
I may be an immature father,
but I'm still your employer.

314
00:18:19,808 --> 00:18:21,768
And as your boss,
I want you on that crew boat tonight

315
00:18:21,851 --> 00:18:22,978
and back in the office by Monday.

316
00:18:23,061 --> 00:18:26,022
- You got that?
- Okay. I quit.

317
00:18:26,564 --> 00:18:29,109
Grace, you can't quit now!

318
00:18:29,192 --> 00:18:30,277
I need you to keep on working.

319
00:18:30,360 --> 00:18:32,737
[ Speaking Chinese Dialect ]

320
00:18:32,821 --> 00:18:35,740
Hi, Harry!

321
00:18:35,824 --> 00:18:36,825
What are you smilin' about?

322
00:18:36,908 --> 00:18:38,994
[ Speaking Chinese Dialect ]

323
00:18:39,077 --> 00:18:42,706
I've been seein' A.J.
for more than five months, Harry.

324
00:18:42,789 --> 00:18:44,499
[ Speaking Chinese Dialect ]

325
00:18:44,582 --> 00:18:47,377
You little hypocrite. I ever held you
back once from doing anything?

326
00:18:47,460 --> 00:18:49,045
What about having a life, Harry?

327
00:18:49,129 --> 00:18:50,422
The first time I got my period,

328
00:18:50,505 --> 00:18:52,841
Rockhound had to take me
into Taipei for Tampax

329
00:18:52,924 --> 00:18:55,218
and then he had to show me
how to use 'em, Harry.

330
00:18:55,302 --> 00:18:57,512
Ho-ho.

331
00:18:57,595 --> 00:19:01,391
I ju... No, I... I told her how to use it.
I didn't show her, Harry.

332
00:19:02,475 --> 00:19:04,519
I was playing with
titanium depth gauges

333
00:19:04,602 --> 00:19:06,354
when I should've been
playing with dolls.

334
00:19:06,438 --> 00:19:10,525
I mean, I learned about the birds and
the bees from Freddy Noonan's tattoos.

335
00:19:10,608 --> 00:19:13,320
Look, I was raised
on roughnecks by you.

336
00:19:13,403 --> 00:19:16,323
And now you get all shocked
and shaken when I fall in love with one.

337
00:19:16,406 --> 00:19:18,241
So who's the hypocrite here,
Harry, huh?

338
00:19:18,325 --> 00:19:19,576
Look at those nice pipes.

339
00:19:19,659 --> 00:19:23,038
- Listen to me, Grace.
- No, you listen to me, Harry. I grew up.

340
00:19:24,080 --> 00:19:27,667
With the proximity
of the asteroid and no prep time,

341
00:19:27,751 --> 00:19:29,627
none of our primary plans can work.

342
00:19:29,711 --> 00:19:33,840
Why don't we just send up 150 nuclear
warheads and blast that rock apart?

343
00:19:33,923 --> 00:19:35,383
Terrible idea.

344
00:19:35,467 --> 00:19:37,510
Was I talkin' to you?

345
00:19:37,594 --> 00:19:39,512
This is Dr. Ronald Quincy
from Research.

346
00:19:39,596 --> 00:19:42,682
Pretty much the smartest man on the
planet. You might wanna listen to him.

347
00:19:42,766 --> 00:19:44,809
General, if you consider your target,

348
00:19:44,893 --> 00:19:47,562
her composition, her dimensions,

349
00:19:47,645 --> 00:19:49,481
her sheer velocity,

350
00:19:49,564 --> 00:19:51,191
you could fire every nuke
you've got on her,

351
00:19:51,274 --> 00:19:54,277
she'll just smile at you
and keep on coming.

352
00:19:54,361 --> 00:19:56,863
You should know that
the president's scientific advisors

353
00:19:56,946 --> 00:20:01,326
are suggesting that a nuclear blast
could change this asteroid's trajectory.

354
00:20:01,409 --> 00:20:05,205
I know the president's chief scientific
advisor. We were at M.I.T. together.

355
00:20:05,288 --> 00:20:07,332
And, in a situation like this...

356
00:20:07,415 --> 00:20:08,917
[ Clears Throat ]
You really don't wanna take the advice

357
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:12,087
from a man who got
a C-minus in astrophysics.

358
00:20:12,796 --> 00:20:17,384
The president's advisors are wrong.
I'm right.

359
00:20:17,967 --> 00:20:20,303
Hitting the rock from
the outside won't do the job.

360
00:20:20,387 --> 00:20:23,515
Imagine a firecracker
in the palm of your hand.

361
00:20:23,598 --> 00:20:27,560
You set it off. What happens?
Burn your hand, right?

362
00:20:27,644 --> 00:20:31,356
You close your fist around
the same firecracker and set it off...

363
00:20:31,439 --> 00:20:35,985
Poof! Your wife's gonna be opening your
ketchup bottles the rest of your life.

364
00:20:36,069 --> 00:20:38,238
Are you suggesting that we blow
this thing up from the inside?

365
00:20:38,321 --> 00:20:40,448
- That's exactly what I'm saying.
- How?

366
00:20:40,532 --> 00:20:42,867
[ Sighs ] We drill.

367
00:20:42,951 --> 00:20:45,078
We bring in the world's best
deep-core driller.

368
00:20:45,286 --> 00:20:47,664
Harry, get up here. We're takin' a hit.

369
00:20:47,747 --> 00:20:49,499
- Get A.J. up here!
- Come on!

370
00:20:49,582 --> 00:20:50,583
Oh, shit!

371
00:20:50,667 --> 00:20:51,793
[ Yelling ]

372
00:20:51,876 --> 00:20:54,087
Send another pipe down! Right now!

373
00:20:54,170 --> 00:20:55,463
[ Yelling Continues ]

374
00:20:55,547 --> 00:20:56,798
It's a gas pocket!

375
00:20:56,881 --> 00:20:59,509
I told you! Am I lucky,
or am I just a genius?

376
00:20:59,592 --> 00:21:02,637
I shut it down for a reason,
you jackass! The relief valve's...

377
00:21:02,720 --> 00:21:05,515
[ Screaming ]

378
00:21:05,598 --> 00:21:09,978
Shut off the number two valve!
Grace, get the clients out of here now!

379
00:21:10,061 --> 00:21:12,313
[ Alarm Blaring ]

380
00:21:12,397 --> 00:21:13,940
No, Daddy!

381
00:21:14,023 --> 00:21:16,192
[ Screaming ]

382
00:21:16,276 --> 00:21:19,195
Chick, get 'em outta here!
Get 'em off the rig now!

383
00:21:24,534 --> 00:21:27,704
- Get the hell down!
- This thing is gonna blow.

384
00:21:31,249 --> 00:21:33,376
[ Screaming ]

385
00:21:33,460 --> 00:21:35,545
[ Yelling Continues ]

386
00:21:35,628 --> 00:21:38,423
Chick, get down now!

387
00:21:38,506 --> 00:21:41,801
Get down!

388
00:21:41,885 --> 00:21:43,011
<i>[Dan ] Three dozen research calls,</i>

389
00:21:43,094 --> 00:21:44,971
<i>and every time,
the same man is recommended.</i>

390
00:21:45,054 --> 00:21:47,307
<i>He's worked on every terrain
this planet can offer.</i>

391
00:21:47,390 --> 00:21:49,559
<i>Whenever they said it couldn't be
drilled, this guy drilled it.</i>

392
00:21:49,642 --> 00:21:53,480
- Everybody all right?
- We struck oil, baby!

393
00:21:53,563 --> 00:21:55,648
Somebody could've got killed
out here today.

394
00:21:55,732 --> 00:21:57,525
You want that on your conscience?

395
00:21:59,694 --> 00:22:01,571
High thumb. You are man, Harry.

396
00:22:01,654 --> 00:22:03,031
Thumbs high.

397
00:22:03,114 --> 00:22:04,407
[ Helicopter Blades Whirring ]

398
00:22:07,076 --> 00:22:08,578
You're fired.

399
00:22:13,583 --> 00:22:16,002
Who's Harry Stamper?

400
00:22:16,085 --> 00:22:18,838
Hey, I'm Harry Stamper.
What's all this about?

401
00:22:18,922 --> 00:22:22,509
Mr. Stamper, I'm General Montgomery,
commander of the Pacific Air Forces.

402
00:22:22,592 --> 00:22:24,636
I've been sent here
by the Secretary of Defense

403
00:22:24,719 --> 00:22:27,847
on direct orders
from the President of the United States.

404
00:22:27,931 --> 00:22:29,015
[ Chuckling ]

405
00:22:29,098 --> 00:22:30,850
It's a matter of urgent national security.

406
00:22:30,934 --> 00:22:34,437
I need you to get on that chopper
right now, no questions asked.

407
00:22:34,521 --> 00:22:36,231
Crazy Willie put you up to this?

408
00:22:36,314 --> 00:22:40,777
I'm afraid I don't know Crazy Willie,
sir. I'm dead serious about this.

409
00:22:42,445 --> 00:22:44,197
- Harry.
- What?

410
00:22:44,280 --> 00:22:46,824
I swear to God,
she never told me her age.

411
00:22:46,908 --> 00:22:49,452
It's all right. Relax. It's about me.

412
00:22:50,537 --> 00:22:52,539
Oh. Forget it!

413
00:22:57,001 --> 00:23:00,964
All right, General,
I'll go with you on one condition.

414
00:23:01,047 --> 00:23:02,966
We're gonna have
to take my daughter along.

415
00:23:05,718 --> 00:23:06,719
What did I do?

416
00:23:06,803 --> 00:23:07,887
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
Where you guys takin' her?

417
00:23:07,971 --> 00:23:10,515
- Sir, stay right here.
- Wh...

418
00:23:10,598 --> 00:23:13,142
Chick, get him paid, get him off the rig!

419
00:23:23,403 --> 00:23:26,489
- Mr. Stamper?
- Yeah, I'm Harry Stamper.

420
00:23:26,573 --> 00:23:28,866
How you doin'? Miss Stamper.

421
00:23:28,950 --> 00:23:30,660
I'm Dan Truman,
Executive Director here.

422
00:23:30,743 --> 00:23:32,912
Listen, on behalf of all of us,
I'd really like to apologize...

423
00:23:32,996 --> 00:23:35,707
Apologize. I don't know if we can take
any more apologies, Mr. Truman.

424
00:23:35,790 --> 00:23:38,710
We've been apologized to
for the last 18-and-a-half hours.

425
00:23:38,793 --> 00:23:41,087
So if you don't mind, how about
if we just get on with it?

426
00:23:41,170 --> 00:23:43,840
You tell us why we're here
at the NASA Space Center.

427
00:23:43,923 --> 00:23:45,758
We should probably talk alone.

428
00:23:45,842 --> 00:23:48,678
Mr. Truman, I don't keep
any secrets from my daughter, Grace.

429
00:23:48,761 --> 00:23:50,638
So whether you tell her now
or I tell her later,

430
00:23:50,722 --> 00:23:52,098
she's gonna find out
one way or the other.

431
00:23:52,181 --> 00:23:53,725
So, why don't we just get on with it?

432
00:23:54,058 --> 00:23:56,227
[ Dan ] So when the Rogue comet
hit the asteroid belt,

433
00:23:56,311 --> 00:23:58,187
it sent shrapnel right for us.

434
00:23:58,271 --> 00:24:00,940
For the next 15 days,
the Earth's in a shooting gallery.

435
00:24:01,024 --> 00:24:05,111
Even if the asteroid itself
hits the water, it's still hitting land.

436
00:24:05,194 --> 00:24:07,780
It'll flash boil
millions of gallons of seawater

437
00:24:07,864 --> 00:24:10,283
and slam into the ocean bedrock.

438
00:24:10,366 --> 00:24:13,786
Now, if it's a Pacific Ocean impact,
which we think it will be,

439
00:24:13,870 --> 00:24:16,789
it'll create a tidal wave three miles high,

440
00:24:16,873 --> 00:24:18,416
travelling at 1,000 miles an hour

441
00:24:18,499 --> 00:24:21,836
covering California
and washing up in Denver.

442
00:24:21,919 --> 00:24:24,756
Japan's gone. Australia's wiped out.

443
00:24:25,465 --> 00:24:28,384
Half the world's population
will be incinerated by the heat blast.

444
00:24:28,509 --> 00:24:31,471
The rest'll freeze to death
from nuclear winter.

445
00:24:31,554 --> 00:24:33,514
[ Whispering ] That's unbelievable.

446
00:24:34,807 --> 00:24:37,727
Well, actually, this is as real as it gets.

447
00:24:40,021 --> 00:24:42,940
Well, it's coming right now.

448
00:24:43,024 --> 00:24:46,069
Right for us at 22,000 miles an hour.

449
00:24:46,152 --> 00:24:48,738
Not a soul on Earth can hide from it.

450
00:25:04,837 --> 00:25:07,256
I take it you're not
alerting everyone like this.

451
00:25:07,340 --> 00:25:10,510
Nobody knows. That's the way it stays.

452
00:25:10,593 --> 00:25:13,346
For the next ten days, there are
only nine telescopes in the world

453
00:25:13,429 --> 00:25:15,932
that can spot the asteroid,
and we control eight of 'em.

454
00:25:16,015 --> 00:25:19,018
The president's classified
this information top secret.

455
00:25:19,102 --> 00:25:20,728
If news like this got out,

456
00:25:20,812 --> 00:25:24,232
there'd be an overnight breakdown
of basic social services worldwide.

457
00:25:24,315 --> 00:25:29,696
Rioting, mass religious hysteria,
total chaos, you can imagine.

458
00:25:29,779 --> 00:25:32,782
Basically the worst parts of the Bible.

459
00:25:35,410 --> 00:25:38,746
Six billion people on the planet.

460
00:25:38,830 --> 00:25:40,790
Why'd you guys call me?

461
00:25:41,624 --> 00:25:42,667
We need you to prep the team

462
00:25:42,750 --> 00:25:44,419
- we're sending up.
- Up?

463
00:25:44,502 --> 00:25:45,712
We'll send them to the asteroid,

464
00:25:45,795 --> 00:25:48,256
they'll land, drill a hole,
they'll drop some nukes,

465
00:25:48,339 --> 00:25:51,050
take off and detonate,
if we can fix this equipment problem.

466
00:25:51,134 --> 00:25:55,888
The drilling unit's a prototype we've
been building for the Mars project.

467
00:25:55,972 --> 00:25:59,183
You, uh... You might recognize the rig.

468
00:26:00,643 --> 00:26:04,522
Yeah, well, I guess
I should recognize it. It's my design.

469
00:26:04,605 --> 00:26:05,815
