00:50:02,000 --> 00:50:05,170
If you wanna replace a member
of the crew, now is the time.

925
00:50:05,253 --> 00:50:08,173
I'll take care of this.
Get him out of the tank, Chick.

926
00:50:12,135 --> 00:50:13,428
You wanna go home? Is that it?

927
00:50:13,511 --> 00:50:15,013
- You wanna be fired?
- No, I don't.

928
00:50:15,096 --> 00:50:16,181
My crew was doing the right thing.

929
00:50:16,264 --> 00:50:17,640
- Your crew?
- Yeah.

930
00:50:17,724 --> 00:50:20,101
Your crew just blew
the transmission, A.J.!

931
00:50:20,185 --> 00:50:22,562
Listen, that NASA computer
is just playin' it safe.

932
00:50:22,645 --> 00:50:24,272
The machine you built,
the rig, could do it.

933
00:50:24,355 --> 00:50:26,649
Shut up. Just shut up! Shut your mouth!

934
00:50:26,733 --> 00:50:30,695
Those men in that room have zero
tolerance for showin' off, hot doggin',

935
00:50:30,778 --> 00:50:34,866
goin' by your gut instinct or
you tryin' to be a hero, you got that?

936
00:50:34,949 --> 00:50:36,784
- Say the words, A.J.!
- I got it!

937
00:50:37,202 --> 00:50:39,412
I want my men
to have tomorrow night off.

938
00:50:39,495 --> 00:50:40,496
What do you mean "off"?

939
00:50:40,580 --> 00:50:42,957
I mean, off. Out of here.
For at least ten hours.

940
00:50:43,041 --> 00:50:44,167
Then we'll go to Kennedy.

941
00:50:44,250 --> 00:50:46,127
Well, there's no possible way
we can do that, Harry.

942
00:50:46,211 --> 00:50:47,545
There's a potentially huge security risk.

943
00:50:47,629 --> 00:50:49,380
What if they talk? What if they get hurt?

944
00:50:49,464 --> 00:50:51,799
What if they're too burnt out
to do the right thing?

945
00:50:51,883 --> 00:50:54,302
What if they get up there,
and they forget what they're fighting for?

946
00:50:54,385 --> 00:50:57,055
You see what's goin' on.
These boys are ready to snap.

947
00:50:57,138 --> 00:50:59,349
They didn't ask to be here.
They got pulled off the street.

948
00:50:59,432 --> 00:51:01,059
For all we know, tomorrow night
could be the last night

949
00:51:01,142 --> 00:51:02,101
they ever see Earth.

950
00:51:02,185 --> 00:51:03,228
I don't think it's too much to ask

951
00:51:03,311 --> 00:51:04,270
to let 'em spend it with their families.

952
00:51:04,354 --> 00:51:05,396
Listen, there's no possible
way we can do that.

953
00:51:05,480 --> 00:51:07,023
You got family, Colonel?

954
00:51:07,106 --> 00:51:08,107
Two girls.

955
00:51:08,191 --> 00:51:11,486
Wouldn't you like to spend tomorrow
with your girls?

956
00:51:12,028 --> 00:51:14,614
I'm not askin' ya. I'm tellin' ya.

957
00:51:14,948 --> 00:51:16,574
Make this happen.

958
00:51:25,667 --> 00:51:29,254
This is a pretty big loan.
Why don't you count the cash?

959
00:51:29,337 --> 00:51:30,922
Nah, this looks like 100 grand to me.

960
00:51:31,005 --> 00:51:34,717
I'm givin' you this at 60 percent.
I hope you know what you're doin',

961
00:51:34,801 --> 00:51:36,928
because I'll bust your head
with a sledgehammer.

962
00:51:37,011 --> 00:51:38,596
You'll get your money back.

963
00:51:38,680 --> 00:51:42,308
You don't look too healthy.
You're not gonna die on me, are ya?

964
00:51:42,392 --> 00:51:46,396
Let's just say, no more than you are.
Thanks, Vic.

965
00:51:53,278 --> 00:51:57,115
<i>Don't wanna close my eyes</i>

966
00:51:57,198 --> 00:51:59,826
<i>I don't wanna fall asleep</i>

967
00:51:59,909 --> 00:52:02,120
<i>'Cause I'd miss you, baby</i>

968
00:52:02,203 --> 00:52:04,163
<i>And I don't wanna miss a thing</i>

969
00:52:04,247 --> 00:52:05,373
You know what I was thinkin'?

970
00:52:05,456 --> 00:52:06,708
What?

971
00:52:08,001 --> 00:52:11,713
I really don't think that the animal
cracker qualifies as a cracker.

972
00:52:11,796 --> 00:52:12,797
Why?

973
00:52:12,880 --> 00:52:14,632
Well, 'cause it's sweet,
which to me suggests cookie.

974
00:52:14,716 --> 00:52:16,509
And, you know,

975
00:52:16,592 --> 00:52:19,262
putting cheese on something
is sort of the defining characteristic

976
00:52:19,345 --> 00:52:21,723
of what makes a cracker a cracker.

977
00:52:21,806 --> 00:52:23,725
I don't know why I thought of that.
I just...

978
00:52:23,808 --> 00:52:26,060
Baby, you have such sweet pillow talk.

979
00:52:26,144 --> 00:52:27,937
I got a little animal cracker,

980
00:52:28,021 --> 00:52:30,565
Discovery Channel thing
happenin' right here.

981
00:52:30,648 --> 00:52:34,902
Watch the gazelle,
as he grazes through the open plains.

982
00:52:36,237 --> 00:52:40,116
Now look, as the cheetah approaches.

983
00:52:40,199 --> 00:52:42,660
Watch, as he stalks his prey.

984
00:52:43,411 --> 00:52:46,080
Now, the gazelle's a little spooked,

985
00:52:46,164 --> 00:52:50,501
and he could head north
to the ample sustenance

986
00:52:50,585 --> 00:52:53,671
provided by
the mountainous peaks above.

987
00:52:53,755 --> 00:52:55,715
[ Imitating Gazelle ]

988
00:52:56,591 --> 00:52:58,301
He could go south.

989
00:53:00,011 --> 00:53:03,765
The gazelle now faces
man's most perilous question:

990
00:53:05,183 --> 00:53:06,517
North...

991
00:53:06,934 --> 00:53:09,020
Or south?

992
00:53:10,396 --> 00:53:14,108
Way down under.

993
00:53:17,653 --> 00:53:18,738
Tune in next week.

994
00:53:18,821 --> 00:53:20,198
[ Giggling ]

995
00:53:21,282 --> 00:53:22,700
Baby,

996
00:53:24,243 --> 00:53:27,789
do you think it's possible
that anyone else in the world

997
00:53:27,872 --> 00:53:31,125
is doing this very same thing
at this very same moment?

998
00:53:31,834 --> 00:53:33,211
I hope so.

999
00:53:34,128 --> 00:53:37,173
Otherwise, what the hell
are we tryin' to save?

1000
00:53:42,178 --> 00:53:45,807
<i>Don't wanna close my eyes</i>

1001
00:53:45,890 --> 00:53:48,393
<i>I don't wanna fall asleep</i>

1002
00:53:48,476 --> 00:53:50,603
<i>'Cause I'd miss you, baby</i>

1003
00:53:50,686 --> 00:53:53,815
<i>And I don't wanna miss a thing</i>

1004
00:53:58,861 --> 00:54:00,029
Hey.

1005
00:54:03,074 --> 00:54:04,742
What are you doing here?

1006
00:54:04,826 --> 00:54:08,413
I was just passin' by on the, uh...
I came...

1007
00:54:13,918 --> 00:54:15,294
Who's he?

1008
00:54:15,837 --> 00:54:17,713
That man's a salesman.

1009
00:54:18,506 --> 00:54:20,341
Would you go inside?

1010
00:54:24,011 --> 00:54:25,471
Thank you.

1011
00:54:26,305 --> 00:54:27,849
[ Door Opens ]

1012
00:54:28,182 --> 00:54:29,642
He got big.

1013
00:54:29,725 --> 00:54:31,144
[ Door Closes ]

1014
00:54:32,728 --> 00:54:35,106
You can't come around like this.

1015
00:54:35,815 --> 00:54:37,817
The court says you can't.

1016
00:54:38,109 --> 00:54:39,360
It confuses him.

1017
00:54:39,444 --> 00:54:41,362
No, I know. I just...

1018
00:54:42,280 --> 00:54:43,990
I wanted to say

1019
00:54:44,532 --> 00:54:46,200
that I'm sorry

1020
00:54:46,993 --> 00:54:48,744
about everything.

1021
00:54:50,830 --> 00:54:54,208
I got somethin' comin' up.
It's somethin' kinda big.

1022
00:54:55,793 --> 00:54:58,129
You just might be proud of me.

1023
00:54:58,212 --> 00:55:01,007
Would you do somethin' for me?
Would you just give him this?

1024
00:55:01,090 --> 00:55:05,011
You don't have to... You don't
have to tell him who it's from. Just...

1025
00:55:13,102 --> 00:55:15,646
<i>Everybody talkin' about
what it is, what it ain't</i>

1026
00:55:15,730 --> 00:55:17,857
<i>Kiss on the devil
and you piss off a saint</i>

1027
00:55:17,940 --> 00:55:20,526
<i>But it can't be love
if you don't have to crawl</i>

1028
00:55:20,610 --> 00:55:23,696
<i>You say you only love him
but you got to have it all</i>

1029
00:55:25,740 --> 00:55:27,992
Hey, Noonan, you need ten grand?

1030
00:55:28,075 --> 00:55:29,660
We gotta put these girls
through college.

1031
00:55:29,744 --> 00:55:31,996
I love this astronaut stuff.

1032
00:55:32,079 --> 00:55:33,748
Good work, if you can get it.

1033
00:55:33,831 --> 00:55:36,501
Yeah, I'm just in town
doin' a little astronaut training.

1034
00:55:36,584 --> 00:55:39,253
Ooh!<i> Astronauta.</i>

1035
00:55:39,337 --> 00:55:41,797
Ah, <i>si.</i> I'm a mission specialist.

1036
00:55:41,923 --> 00:55:44,258
Yes, and what's that mean?

1037
00:55:44,550 --> 00:55:46,052
I don't know.

1038
00:55:47,887 --> 00:55:51,474
Hey! Who the hell
do you think you guys are?

1039
00:55:51,557 --> 00:55:52,850
You're hoggin' all the action.

1040
00:55:52,934 --> 00:55:56,187
Hey, pinhead.
Why don't you go find your own party?

1041
00:55:56,270 --> 00:55:57,688
Why don't you spread the wealth, pal?

1042
00:55:57,772 --> 00:55:59,440
Here. Why don't
you go buy yourself a neck?

1043
00:55:59,524 --> 00:56:01,067
Hey, Mr. Clean!

1044
00:56:01,150 --> 00:56:02,985
[ Women Screaming ]

1045
00:56:03,569 --> 00:56:04,654
[ Yelling ]

1046
00:56:05,988 --> 00:56:07,865
Call NASA! They'll confirm it!
We're astronauts!

1047
00:56:07,949 --> 00:56:09,075
Get over there. Yeah, yeah.

1048
00:56:09,158 --> 00:56:11,285
- Yeah, we're astronauts!
- Yeah, we're all astronauts.

1049
00:56:11,369 --> 00:56:14,413
You are so messing
with national security right now, man.

1050
00:56:14,497 --> 00:56:16,916
You are fired tomorrow morning.
I'm telling ya.

1051
00:56:16,999 --> 00:56:19,043
I'll get the C.I.A. and the F.B.I.

1052
00:56:19,126 --> 00:56:20,962
You'll be workin' security at Toys 'R' Us.

1053
00:56:21,045 --> 00:56:23,047
- Oh, oh, baby, no, no. No, no!
- Bye-bye, little astronaut.

1054
00:56:23,130 --> 00:56:24,549
Oh, don't leave, baby. No, no, no.

1055
00:56:24,632 --> 00:56:26,634
See, I'm goin' into space,
and I'm not comin' back.

1056
00:56:31,305 --> 00:56:33,140
It's coming in at 30,000 miles an hour!

1057
00:56:33,224 --> 00:56:35,184
Give me a projected impact.

1058
00:56:35,268 --> 00:56:36,727
East Asia, 11 minutes.

1059
00:56:36,811 --> 00:56:40,147
- We're gonna have to warn...
- Warn who? The entire South Pacific?

1060
00:56:46,487 --> 00:56:49,073
[ People Chattering In Chinese Dialect ]

1061
00:56:55,705 --> 00:56:58,124
[ Loud Rumbling ]

1062
00:57:05,006 --> 00:57:07,758
[ People Screaming ]

1063
00:57:30,031 --> 00:57:31,490
[ Phone Rings ]

1064
00:57:33,743 --> 00:57:35,786
So the whole world knows.

1065
00:57:37,955 --> 00:57:40,875
Tell me you've never let
anybody down before.

1066
00:57:41,375 --> 00:57:43,753
I never quit yet. How's that?

1067
00:57:44,420 --> 00:57:46,547
I guess that'll have to do.

1068
00:57:47,840 --> 00:57:49,550
You know somethin'?

1069
00:57:50,343 --> 00:57:52,928
I still remember the first,
middle and last name

1070
00:57:53,012 --> 00:57:55,306
of every guy that qualified
for the astronaut programme

1071
00:57:55,389 --> 00:57:57,600
first year I was here. Thanks.

1072
00:57:58,017 --> 00:58:00,561
I went into the engineering programme.

1073
00:58:00,895 --> 00:58:02,313
Kinda had to.

1074
00:58:02,563 --> 00:58:04,565
But boy, I wanted to go up there.

1075
00:58:04,649 --> 00:58:08,653
I wanted to be one of those guys
with a mission patch on my arm.

1076
00:58:09,945 --> 00:58:12,281
I tell you, I'd be on that shuttle
with you, Harry, if I could.

1077
00:58:12,365 --> 00:58:13,699
[ Laughs ]

1078
00:58:17,078 --> 00:58:20,748
You don't want to be up
in that shuttle any more than I do.

1079
00:58:21,916 --> 00:58:23,751
Good luck in Florida tomorrow.

1080
00:58:23,876 --> 00:58:25,628
<i>[Female Newscaster#1 ]
The death of50,000 people</i>

1081
00:58:25,711 --> 00:58:28,005
<i>in Shanghai yesterday has rattled...</i>

1082
00:58:28,089 --> 00:58:29,340
<i>[ Male Newscaster#1 ]
A French satellite has tracked</i>

1083
00:58:29,423 --> 00:58:31,300
<i>an object in space...</i>

1084
00:58:31,384 --> 00:58:32,510
<i>[Female Newscaster#2]
Sources are estimating</i>

1085
00:58:32,593 --> 00:58:34,095
<i>that the tidal wave was five...</i>

1086
00:58:34,178 --> 00:58:35,971
<i>[ Male Newscaster#2]
This is CNN, live in Florida.</i>

1087
00:58:36,055 --> 00:58:39,600
<i>We have just learned that NASA
is on a full-scale military alert.</i>

1088
00:58:39,684 --> 00:58:42,228
<i>They're calling this a global killer.</i>

1089
00:58:42,311 --> 00:58:43,312
<i>[Female Newscaster#3]
The government has been</i>

1090
00:58:43,396 --> 00:58:44,355
<i>very tight-lipped throughout this...</i>

1091
00:58:44,438 --> 00:58:45,981
<i>[Female Newscaster#4 ]
The Pentagon is getting involved</i>

1092
00:58:46,065 --> 00:58:47,400
<i>at this point with some kind of a project</i>

1093
00:58:47,483 --> 00:58:50,361
<i>involving NASA
and perhaps a shuttle mission...</i>

1094
00:58:50,444 --> 00:58:52,738
Senior Pentagon officials
refused comment,

1095
00:58:52,822 --> 00:58:54,115
adding fuel to the speculation

1096
00:58:54,198 --> 00:58:57,201
that there could be
a very serious problem.

1097
00:58:57,284 --> 00:58:59,036
<i>[ Truman ]
We have a special team of astronauts</i>

1098
00:58:59,120 --> 00:59:01,080
<i>that arrived in Florida this evening.</i>

1099
00:59:01,163 --> 00:59:03,416
<i>NASA's in emergency
launch preparation</i>

1100
00:59:03,499 --> 00:59:05,543
<i>in cooperation with Russian, Japanese</i>

1101
00:59:05,626 --> 00:59:06,711
<i>and French space agencies</i>

1102
00:59:06,794 --> 00:59:10,131
<i>on the most massive joint
space venture in history.</i>

1103
00:59:18,472 --> 00:59:19,640
Gracie?

1104
00:59:29,191 --> 00:59:30,693
Got your note.

1105
00:59:32,027 --> 00:59:33,070
What're you doin' out here, honey?

1106
00:59:33,154 --> 00:59:35,156
Um, just thinkin'.

1107
00:59:36,407 --> 00:59:39,493
- Yeah.
- I, um, want to apologize to you for...

1108
00:59:39,577 --> 00:59:42,747
Oh, no, Grace, stop.
You don't have to apologize at all.

1109
00:59:42,830 --> 00:59:44,039
I... I...

1110
00:59:46,125 --> 00:59:48,544
I shouldn't have dragged you
around on all those oil rigs.

1111
00:59:48,627 --> 00:59:49,879
I just...

1112
00:59:51,464 --> 00:59:53,632
I don't think that I did
the right thing with you.

1113
00:59:53,716 --> 00:59:56,594
You're wrong. I love my life.

1114
00:59:57,553 --> 00:59:59,805
I love everything about my life.

1115
00:59:59,889 --> 01:00:02,850
And I don't blame you
for my mother leaving.

1116
01:00:05,311 --> 01:00:06,937
She left us both.

1117
01:00:08,731 --> 01:00:10,357
And I love you.

1118
01:00:10,691 --> 01:00:13,611
And don't talk
like you're not comin' back.

1119
01:00:14,945 --> 01:00:17,364
Promise me that you'll come back.

1120
01:00:18,532 --> 01:00:19,825
Okay.

1121
01:00:20,034 --> 01:00:21,660
Say, "I promise."

1122
01:00:23,245 --> 01:00:25,039
I promise, Grace.

1123
01:00:28,959 --> 01:00:31,378
It's gonna be all right, Grace.

1124
01:00:35,508 --> 01:00:37,927
If it's not too much trouble,

1125
01:00:38,010 --> 01:00:40,387
can you please
bring my fiancée home with you?

1126
01:00:40,471 --> 01:00:42,223
Oh, Jesus.

1127
01:00:52,775 --> 01:00:55,569
<i>The president will be addressing
the nation and all of you personally</i>

1128
01:00:55,653 --> 01:00:56,904
<i>within the hour.</i>

1129
01:01:24,557 --> 01:01:26,100
Astronauts.

1130
01:01:33,107 --> 01:01:35,860
I'll see you in a couple days, honey.

1131
01:01:41,282 --> 01:01:44,910
<i>[ Singing]All my bags are packed</i>

1132
01:01:44,994 --> 01:01:46,787
<i>I'm ready to go</i>

1133
01:01:48,122 --> 01:01:49,915
<i>I'm standin' here outside your door</i>

1134
01:01:49,999 --> 01:01:51,667
[ Humming ]

1135
01:01:52,751 --> 01:01:54,545
<i>I hate to wake you up</i>

1136
01:01:55,671 --> 01:01:57,798
<i>To say goodbye</i>

1137
01:01:58,173 --> 01:02:02,177
<i>So kiss me and smile for me</i>

1138
01:02:02,595 --> 01:02:05,639
<i>Let me know you'll wait for me</i>

1139
01:02:05,723 --> 01:02:09,935
<i>Hold me like you'll never let me go</i>

1140
01:02:10,436 --> 01:02:11,478
[ Grunting ]

1141
01:02:11,562 --> 01:02:13,480
<i>'Cause I'm leavin'</i>

1142
01:02:13,564 --> 01:02:16,025
<i>On a jet plane</i>

1143
01:02:16,108 --> 01:02:18,986
<i>Don't know when I'll be back again</i>

1144
01:02:19,069 --> 01:02:23,324
<i>Leavin' on a jet plane</i>

1145
01:02:23,407 --> 01:02:26,702
<i>I don't know when I'll be back again</i>

1146
01:02:26,785 --> 01:02:30,581
<i>Leavin' on a jet plane</i>

1147
01:02:30,664 --> 01:02:33,584
<i>I don't know when I'll be back again</i>

1148
01:02:33,667 --> 01:02:35,336
<i>Leavin' on a jet plane
Don't know when I'll be back again</i>

1149
01:02:35,419 --> 01:02:39,465
So, Truman, this is who you found
to save the planet.

1150
01:02:40,049 --> 01:02:41,759
- Frost, you good to go?
- Mm-hmm. One... One sec.

1151
01:02:41,842 --> 01:02:42,885
<i>Leavin' on a jet plane</i>

1152
01:02:42,968 --> 01:02:44,887
That boy don't take anything seriously.

1153
01:02:44,970 --> 01:02:47,890
Yeah. Reminds me of a guy
I used to know.

1154
01:02:48,432 --> 01:02:50,267
<i>Aah</i>

1155
01:02:50,351 --> 01:02:52,227
<i>Leavin' on a jet plane</i>

1156
01:02:52,311 --> 01:02:53,771
<i>I don't know when I'll be back again</i>

1157
01:02:53,854 --> 01:02:55,230
I'm marrying you.

1158
01:02:55,314 --> 01:02:56,315
Bet your ass you are.

1159
01:02:56,398 --> 01:02:59,026
<i>Leavin' on a jet plane</i>

1160
01:02:59,568 --> 01:03:01,987
<i>I don't know when I'll be back again</i>

1161
01:03:06,533 --> 01:03:08,827
[ Crowd Cheering ]

1162
01:03:17,711 --> 01:03:19,588
<i>I address you tonight,</i>

1163
01:03:20,422 --> 01:03:23,300
<i>not as the President
of the United States,</i>

1164
01:03:24,760 --> 01:03:27,137
<i>not as the leader of a country,</i>

1165
01:03:27,596 --> 01:03:29,807
<i>but as a citizen of humanity.</i>

1166
01:03:32,893 --> 01:03:36,063
<i>We are faced
with the very gravest of challenges.</i>

1167
01:03:38,065 --> 01:03:42,778
<i>The Bible calls this day
Armageddon, the end of all things.</i>

1168
01:03:44,071 --> 01:03:47,366
<i>And yet, for the first time,</i>

1169
01:03:48,242 --> 01:03:49,994
<i>in the history of the planet,</i>

1170
01:03:50,077 --> 01:03:53,163
<i>a species has the technology</i>

1171
01:03:53,247 --> 01:03:55,499
<i>to prevent its own extinction.</i>

1172
01:03:55,582 --> 01:03:56,917
<i>[ Translator On TV]</i>

1173
01:03:57,001 --> 01:03:59,795
<i>All of you praying with us need to know</i>

1174
01:04:01,130 --> 01:04:05,426
<i>that everything that can be done
to prevent this disaster</i>

1175
01:04:05,509 --> 01:04:07,928
<i>is being called into service.</i>

1176
01:04:10,347 --> 01:04:13,809
<i>The human thirst for excellence,</i>

1177
01:04:13,892 --> 01:04:14,852
<i>[ Translator On Radio ]</i>

1178
01:04:14,935 --> 01:04:16,395
<i>knowledge,</i>

1179
01:04:17,604 --> 01:04:20,607
<i>every step up the ladder of science,</i>

1180
01:04:21,942 --> 01:04:26,113
<i>every adventurous reach into space,</i>

1181
01:04:26,196 --> 01:04:30,200
<i>all of our combined
modern technologies and imaginations,</i>

1182
01:04:30,284 --> 01:04:34,204
<i>even the wars that we've fought,
have provided us the tools...</i>

1183
01:04:34,288 --> 01:04:36,457
<i>to wage this terrible battle.</i>

1184
01:04:37,875 --> 01:04:39,668
<i>Through all the chaos
that is our history,</i>

1185
01:04:39,752 --> 01:04:40,753
<i>[ Translator On TV]</i>

1186
01:04:40,836 --> 01:04:43,714
<i>through all of the wrongs
and the discord,</i>

1187
01:04:43,797 --> 01:04:45,758
<i>through all of the pain and suffering,</i>

1188
01:04:45,841 --> 01:04:47,885
<i>through all of our times,</i>

1189
01:04:47,968 --> 01:04:50,220
<i>there is one thing
that has nourished our souls...</i>

1190
01:04:50,304 --> 01:04:52,890
Mom, that salesman's on TV.

1191
01:04:52,973 --> 01:04:56,101
<i>...and elevated our species
above its origins,</i>

1192
01:04:56,185 --> 01:04:58,187
<i>and that is our courage.</i>

1193
01:04:58,812 --> 01:05:01,899
<i>Dreams of an entire planet
are focused tonight</i>

1194
01:05:01,982 --> 01:05:04,651
<i>on those 14 brave souls</i>

1195
01:05:05,444 --> 01:05:07,529
<i>travelling into the heavens.</i>

1196
01:05:07,780 --> 01:05:09,907
That man's not a salesman.

1197
01:05:09,990 --> 01:05:11,241
That's your daddy.

1198
01:05:11,325 --> 01:05:12,409
<i>And may we all,</i>

1199
01:05:12,493 --> 01:05:15,996
<i>citizens the world over,
see these events through.</i>

1200
01:05:17,039 --> 01:05:20,375
<i>Godspeed and good luck to you.</i>

1201
01:05:27,883 --> 01:05:30,219
<i>Freedom</i> crew.<i> Independence</i> crew.

1202
01:05:35,641 --> 01:05:36,934
How ya feelin'?

1203
01:05:37,017 --> 01:05:40,521
Uh, good, you know.
I mean, considering I've never been

1204
01:05:40,604 --> 01:05:43,440
this scared in my entire life.
I... You know...

1205
01:05:43,524 --> 01:05:47,194
Listen. Once you get up there,
you're gonna be on your own.

1206
01:05:47,277 --> 01:05:48,821
If anything should happen,
I just wanted to...

1207
01:05:48,904 --> 01:05:52,533
I know, Harry.
I'll, uh, try not to disappoint you.

1208
01:05:56,662 --> 01:05:58,872
Take care of yourself, kid.

1209
01:06:03,669 --> 01:06:06,046
<i>[ Man #1 ]</i> Freedom's <i>on the bridge.</i>

1210
01:06:06,130 --> 01:06:09,883
<i>Attention in the firing room.
Oxidizer loading is complete.</i>

1211
01:06:11,176 --> 01:06:12,636
<i>[ Man #2]</i> Independence <i>on the bridge.</i>

1212
01:06:12,719 --> 01:06:14,513
<i>[ Man #1 ]Attention all personnel.</i>

1213
01:06:14,596 --> 01:06:17,558
<i>We are T minus two hours
to the programme goal.</i>

1214
01:06:26,525 --> 01:06:28,527
- Hey, Harry.
- [ Harry ] Yeah, Rock?

1215
01:06:28,610 --> 01:06:31,905
You know, we're sittin' on four million
pounds of fuel, one nuclear weapon

1216
01:06:31,989 --> 01:06:34,992
and a thing that has
270,000 moving parts

1217
01:06:35,075 --> 01:06:36,660
built by the lowest bidder.

1218
01:06:36,743 --> 01:06:37,703
[ Grunts ]

1219
01:06:37,786 --> 01:06:40,289
Makes you feel good, doesn't it?

1220
01:06:40,372 --> 01:06:41,498
Yeah.

1221
01:06:43,959 --> 01:06:46,086
- How ya doin', Oscar?
- Great.

1222
01:06:46,420 --> 01:06:48,922
I got that excited, scared feelin',

1223
01:06:49,006 --> 01:06:51,884
like 98 percent excited,
2 percent scared.

1224
01:06:52,301 --> 01:06:54,011
Maybe more. It could be 2...

1225
01:06:54,094 --> 01:06:56,054
It could be 98 percent scared,
2 percent excited.

1226
01:06:56,138 --> 01:06:59,808
But that's what makes it so intense,
is it's so confused.

1227
01:06:59,892 --> 01:07:01,852
I can't really figure it out.

1228
01:07:01,935 --> 01:07:04,521
Will you make mine really tight,
'cause I don't want to fall out?

1229
01:07:04,605 --> 01:07:07,107
I mean, almost to the point
of cutting off circulation.

1230
01:07:07,191 --> 01:07:08,483
[ Harnesses Clattering ]

1231
01:07:08,567 --> 01:07:09,610
Ow.

1232
01:07:10,777 --> 01:07:13,113
It must be a comfort to know that
if the space programme goes under,

1233
01:07:13,197 --> 01:07:15,115
you can always get a job
at Helga's House of Pain, huh?

1234
01:07:15,490 --> 01:07:18,035
All right. Flight directors
on with the go/no-go for launch.

1235
01:07:18,118 --> 01:07:19,328
- Retro.
- Go flight.

1236
01:07:19,411 --> 01:07:20,704
- Booster.
- Go flight.

1237
01:07:20,787 --> 01:07:21,747
- Ecos.
- Go flight.

1238
01:07:21,830 --> 01:07:23,207
- Trajectory.
- Go flight.

1239
01:07:23,290 --> 01:07:24,625
- FIDO.
- Go flight.

1240
01:07:24,708 --> 01:07:25,792
- EVA.
- Go flight.

1241
01:07:25,876 --> 01:07:27,377
- CAPCOM <i>Freedom.</i>
- Go flight.

1242
01:07:27,461 --> 01:07:29,796
- CAPCOM <i>Independence.</i>
- Go flight.

1243
01:07:29,880 --> 01:07:33,008
All right, ladies and gentlemen,
it's pucker time.

1244
01:07:33,091 --> 01:07:35,552
Independence <i>and</i> Freedom,
<i>this is Kennedy firing room.</i>

1245
01:07:35,636 --> 01:07:37,304
<i>We're T minus one minute.</i>

1246
01:07:37,387 --> 01:07:40,307
All crew members,
close and lock your visors.

1247
01:07:41,266 --> 01:07:45,103
Independence, <i>this is launch control.</i>
<i>Be advised, we're in a smooth count.</i>

1248
01:07:45,187 --> 01:07:48,398
T minus 31.
You're go for auto-sequence start.

1249
01:07:48,482 --> 01:07:51,068
<i>P.L.T.s, perform your A.P.U. pre-start.</i>

1250
01:07:51,151 --> 01:07:54,196
Okay, gentlemen,
you're our warriors up there.

1251
01:07:55,322 --> 01:07:56,490
God be with you.

1252
01:07:56,573 --> 01:07:59,243
<i>You're already heroes.
Just sit back and enjoy the ride.</i>

1253
01:07:59,326 --> 01:08:00,744
<i>[ Man Chattering On Radio ]</i>

1254
01:08:00,827 --> 01:08:02,871
<i>We're T minus 20 seconds.</i>

1255
01:08:04,248 --> 01:08:05,749
<i>[ Chattering Continues]</i>

1256
01:08:05,832 --> 01:08:09,503
<i>Ten. Nine. Eight. Seven.</i>

1257
01:08:10,462 --> 01:08:13,757
<i>Four. Three. Two. One.</i>

1258
01:08:16,176 --> 01:08:17,261
[ Roaring ]

1259
01:08:17,344 --> 01:08:18,345
<i>We have main engine start.</i>

1260
01:08:18,428 --> 01:08:21,181
<i>- We have booster ignition.</i>
- We're going.

1261
01:08:22,015 --> 01:08:23,433
<i>And liftoff.</i>

1262
01:08:33,277 --> 01:08:35,487
Freedom, <i>this is flight deck.</i>

1263
01:08:36,613 --> 01:08:40,242
<i>[ Sharp On Radio ]
Roger,</i> Freedom.<i> You're looking good.</i>

1264
01:08:51,545 --> 01:08:53,672
We have go for <i>Independence.</i>

1265
01:08:53,755 --> 01:08:56,216
<i>Three. Two. One.</i>

1266
01:08:56,633 --> 01:08:58,385
Independence,
<i>we have booster ignition.</i>

1267
01:08:58,468 --> 01:08:59,845
<i>[ Chattering Continues]</i>

1268
01:08:59,928 --> 01:09:01,263
<i>We have liftoff.</i>

1269
01:09:01,346 --> 01:09:02,973
We are cooking, Houston.

1270
01:09:25,078 --> 01:09:27,539
Houston, the tower is clear.
They're all yours.

1271
01:09:27,622 --> 01:09:29,166
[ Cheering ]

1272
01:09:29,458 --> 01:09:30,834
[ Shuttles Roaring ]

1273
01:09:30,917 --> 01:09:32,502
Heads up, everybody. They're ours now.

1274
01:09:32,586 --> 01:09:33,837
<i>All engines are go.</i>

1275
01:09:33,920 --> 01:09:35,922
Keep a sharp eye out on both of 'em.

1276
01:09:36,006 --> 01:09:38,175
<i>[ Radio Chatter Continues]</i>

1277
01:09:43,138 --> 01:09:45,599
<i>[ Sharp] Start roll manoeuvre.</i>

1278
01:09:55,734 --> 01:09:57,069
Two good roll programmes.

1279
01:09:57,152 --> 01:09:58,945
- One down.
- Independence, <i>we have max cue.</i>

1280
01:09:59,029 --> 01:10:01,615
Roger, Control. We are a max cue.

1281
01:10:03,116 --> 01:10:04,201
S.R.B. sep...

1282
01:10:04,284 --> 01:10:05,619
[ Engines Roaring ]

1283
01:10:09,706 --> 01:10:11,500
We are single-engine, press, demi-go.

1284
01:10:11,583 --> 01:10:13,210
<i>Copy, press, demi-go.</i>

1285
01:10:13,293 --> 01:10:15,670
Houston, this is a kick-ass ride!

1286
01:10:21,551 --> 01:10:24,388
Freedom, <i>this is Houston.</i>
<i>Main engine cut out on schedule. Out.</i>

1287
01:10:24,471 --> 01:10:26,890
[ Engines Cut Out ]

1288
01:10:34,272 --> 01:10:36,441
Freedom, <i>stats are good.</i>

1289
01:10:40,612 --> 01:10:42,906
Independence,
<i>telemetry is up and running.</i>

1290
01:10:42,989 --> 01:10:44,116
Oh, my God.

1291
01:10:44,199 --> 01:10:48,078
This is space! Course, we're just
in the beginning part of space.

1292
01:10:48,161 --> 01:10:50,580
We... We haven't gotten
to outer space yet.

1293
01:10:50,664 --> 01:10:52,874
Roger, Houston. We have a visual
on the Russian space station.

1294
01:10:52,958 --> 01:10:54,835
Initiating retro burn.

1295
01:10:56,628 --> 01:10:58,588
Gentlemen, remember
the Russian space station

1296
01:10:58,672 --> 01:11:00,298
has been up there for 11 years.

1297
01:11:00,382 --> 01:11:02,259
<i>Most of us don't have cars that old.</i>

1298
01:11:02,342 --> 01:11:03,301
<i>Now, the cosmonaut on board</i>

1299
01:11:03,385 --> 01:11:06,513
<i>has been on that tin can
for 18 months, alone.</i>

1300
01:11:09,433 --> 01:11:11,977
<i>So don't be surprised if he's a little... off.</i>

1301
01:11:12,060 --> 01:11:13,353
Independence, <i>we're gonna put you...</i>

1302
01:11:13,437 --> 01:11:15,272
All right, crew.
Let's exit these flight suits.

1303
01:11:15,355 --> 01:11:16,398
[ Laughing ]

1304
01:11:17,274 --> 01:11:18,942
[ Russian Accent ] Hello.

1305
01:11:19,025 --> 01:11:22,571
This is Russian space station.
Can you hear me?

1306
01:11:22,988 --> 01:11:23,947
[ Speaks Russian ]

1307
01:11:24,030 --> 01:11:25,949
We copy, Russian space station.
This is Houston.

1308
01:11:26,032 --> 01:11:29,536
<i>I'm ready to fire my thrusters any time.</i>

1309
01:11:29,828 --> 01:11:33,039
<i>- Stand by.
- Okay. I'm not going anywhere.</i>

1310
01:11:33,123 --> 01:11:35,792
<i>We have a go.
Initiate gravitational spin.</i>

1311
01:11:35,876 --> 01:11:37,127
<i>[ Chattering On Radio ]</i>

1312
01:11:37,210 --> 01:11:38,879
[ Thrusters Roaring ]

1313
01:11:43,383 --> 01:11:45,427
<i>You are maxed at 40-percent spin.</i>

1314
01:11:45,510 --> 01:11:46,720
[ Moans ]

1315
01:11:47,846 --> 01:11:49,890
Okay, Houston.

1316
01:11:50,724 --> 01:11:54,895
I can feel I'm having gravity.

1317
01:11:55,604 --> 01:11:58,315
All right, gentlemen.
We're gonna dock in a minute.

1318
01:11:58,398 --> 01:11:59,483
Now, the Russian space station

1319
01:11:59,566 --> 01:12:00,942
- has fired her rockets...
- Whee!

1320
01:12:01,026 --> 01:12:03,111
...to simulate gravity
and let us work faster.

1321
01:12:03,195 --> 01:12:05,155
It's gonna make you queasy,
so prepare yourself.

1322
01:12:05,238 --> 01:12:07,741
Well, it's about time.
I haven't thrown up in about an hour.

1323
01:12:07,824 --> 01:12:09,326
[ Laughing ]

1324
01:12:12,704 --> 01:12:15,790
<i>Initiating first phase
of docking procedure.</i>

1325
01:12:16,124 --> 01:12:18,752
- Switching to manual.
- Manual override.

1326
01:12:24,508 --> 01:12:28,345
One foot per second. Let's take this
slow and do it right, folks.

1327
01:12:28,428 --> 01:12:29,846
Twenty feet.

1328
01:12:30,931 --> 01:12:32,432
[ Blipping ]

1329
01:12:32,599 --> 01:12:33,767
Ten feet.

1330
01:12:33,850 --> 01:12:35,810
<i>Looking good on radar.</i>

1331
01:12:37,020 --> 01:12:38,396
Five feet.

1332
01:12:39,147 --> 01:12:41,441
[ Clanking, Hissing ]

1333
01:12:42,275 --> 01:12:45,028
Locks are engaged. Fuel teams, let's go.

1334
01:12:46,738 --> 01:12:48,990
Freedom, <i>telemetry is looking good.</i>

1335
01:12:49,074 --> 01:12:50,158
[ Hissing ]

1336
01:12:50,242 --> 01:12:51,993
We have soft dock.

1337
01:12:52,077 --> 01:12:54,120
[ Sharp ] Fuel teams, prepare to unload.

1338
01:12:58,833 --> 01:13:00,544
All right, gentlemen, watch your heads.

1339
01:13:00,627 --> 01:13:02,546
Let's go, <i>Independence.</i>

1340
01:13:06,007 --> 01:13:07,342
Colonel.

1341
01:13:10,845 --> 01:13:12,973
<i>[ Russian Folk Music]</i>

1342
01:13:17,644 --> 01:13:20,355
Where is he? Anybody home?

1343
01:13:21,314 --> 01:13:23,275
Welcome, everybody!

1344
01:13:25,694 --> 01:13:27,654
I am not gas station.

1345
01:13:27,737 --> 01:13:31,032
This is sophisticated laboratory.
I'm in charge.

1346
01:13:31,324 --> 01:13:33,743
So do not be touching anything.

1347
01:13:33,827 --> 01:13:36,746
- I need one... I need you.
- Go with him.

1348
01:13:36,830 --> 01:13:39,457
I need you. Hurry up. Hurry up.
Come on. Come on.

1349
01:13:39,541 --> 01:13:42,669
It's very important
you watch the fuel gauge, okay?

1350
01:13:42,752 --> 01:13:44,212
Put on cold suit.

1351
01:13:44,296 --> 01:13:45,797
<i>- Countdown clock will hold at...
- Copy that, Houston.</i>

1352
01:13:45,880 --> 01:13:47,132
<i>Prepping for fuel transfer.</i>

1353
01:13:47,215 --> 01:13:49,509
<i>Countdown clock will hold
at T minus 20 minutes and...</i>

1354
01:13:49,926 --> 01:13:51,928
Fuel pod is down there.

1355
01:13:52,012 --> 01:13:53,930
It's down here, huh? Great.

1356
01:13:54,014 --> 01:13:56,182
[ Hissing ]

1357
01:13:56,558 --> 01:13:58,351
[ All Chattering ]

1358
01:14:04,691 --> 01:14:07,569
Okay, let's connect these fuel lines.

1359
01:14:09,696 --> 01:14:12,699
<i>Freedom</i> on the left,
<i>Independence</i> on the right.

1360
01:14:12,782 --> 01:14:15,243
All right. We're goin' left here.

1361
01:14:16,494 --> 01:14:19,956
To the right is fuel gauge.
You watch the fuel gauge.

1362
01:14:20,040 --> 01:14:22,375
One fifty, okay. One sixty, okay.

1363
01:14:22,459 --> 01:14:26,087
Two hundred,
bad disaster for space station.

1364
01:14:26,713 --> 01:14:32,093
So if you watch 200, you call for Lev,
on, and you see here number one. Off.

1365
01:14:32,177 --> 01:14:34,804
You ask for Lev. And you pull
this down, all the way down.

1366
01:14:34,888 --> 01:14:36,181
What's Lev?

1367
01:14:36,264 --> 01:14:39,643
I am Lev Andropov,
colonel of Russian space agency.

1368
01:14:39,726 --> 01:14:41,895
In Russia I'm a very big man.

1369
01:14:43,521 --> 01:14:44,814
We're ready to transfer.

1370
01:14:44,898 --> 01:14:46,775
I'm coming. No problem.

1371
01:14:46,858 --> 01:14:49,277
[ All Chattering ]

1372
01:14:49,361 --> 01:14:51,905
You. You. You there!

1373
01:14:52,739 --> 01:14:55,367
- Hard locked.
- Ready for transfusion!

1374
01:14:55,909 --> 01:14:56,910
[ Beeps ]

1375
01:14:56,993 --> 01:14:59,079
[ Hissing ]

1376
01:15:04,125 --> 01:15:06,044
<i>[ Lev] Fuel is pumping.</i>

1377
01:15:09,923 --> 01:15:12,467
Hey, Lev, the, uh...
The... The pressure's climbing.

1378
01:15:12,550 --> 01:15:14,094
<i>[A.J. Continues, Radio Static Hissing]</i>

1379
01:15:14,177 --> 01:15:16,513
Still, we're on fuel transference.

1380
01:15:16,596 --> 01:15:19,182
Don't touch my uncle. You know?

1381
01:15:19,265 --> 01:15:20,892
He's a genius of my family.

1382
01:15:20,975 --> 01:15:22,018
[ Hissing ]

1383
01:15:22,102 --> 01:15:25,897
Lev! Can anybody hear me?
Guys? Hello, guys!

1384
01:15:25,980 --> 01:15:26,981
[ No Audio ]

1385
01:15:27,065 --> 01:15:28,525
He used to work for a big bomb factory.

1386
01:15:28,608 --> 01:15:30,527
He used to make the tip of the bomb,

1387
01:15:30,610 --> 01:15:34,864
the thing that finds, uh, New York
or Washington, you know?

1388
01:15:35,323 --> 01:15:36,491
Ooh.

1389
01:15:36,574 --> 01:15:38,910
Check your hoses.
We got some thermal variation.

1390
01:15:38,993 --> 01:15:41,913
Stamper, let's look at the couplings,
back on the shuttle.

1391
01:15:43,998 --> 01:15:46,126
Okay. Shut down. Uh...

1392
01:15:46,960 --> 01:15:48,461
[ Grunting ]

1393
01:15:50,505 --> 01:15:52,507
[ Motors Grinding Down ]

1394
01:15:52,590 --> 01:15:54,884
Uh... Guys!

1395
01:15:55,802 --> 01:15:57,971
[ Sharp ] What's that noise?

1396
01:15:58,972 --> 01:16:01,307
Oh, no! God!

1397
01:16:04,310 --> 01:16:05,854
What is it?

1398
01:16:06,312 --> 01:16:08,857
[ Shouting In Russian ] Leak! Leak!

1399
01:16:10,316 --> 01:16:13,319
Get your men back to the shuttle! Go!

1400
01:16:14,612 --> 01:16:17,574
Go! Hurry up! Get out of there!

1401
01:16:17,657 --> 01:16:20,034
You know, this really smarts!

1402
01:16:20,118 --> 01:16:22,036
Pull lever!

1403
01:16:22,120 --> 01:16:23,788
This is the lever!

1404
01:16:24,247 --> 01:16:26,082
Colonel, we must get him out of there!

1405
01:16:26,166 --> 01:16:28,501
A.J., come on out!

1406
01:16:29,544 --> 01:16:31,254
Aah! Aah!

1407
01:16:31,546 --> 01:16:33,214
Hurry! Hurry!

1408
01:16:35,842 --> 01:16:37,677
Emergency break away!

1409
01:16:38,428 --> 01:16:40,555
We got a fire in the fuel pod!

1410
01:16:43,850 --> 01:16:45,101
- Come on!
- Come on!

1411
01:16:45,185 --> 01:16:47,854
Get in here! A.J.'s stuck in the fuel pod!

1412
01:16:49,898 --> 01:16:50,982
We're losing it!

1413
01:16:51,065 --> 01:16:52,776
[ All Shouting ]

1414
01:16:57,697 --> 01:16:59,240
[ All Shouting ]

1415
01:17:03,745 --> 01:17:07,207
Control, this is <i>Independence.</i>
I am seeing vibration...

1416
01:17:07,457 --> 01:17:08,833
[ All Shouting ]

1417
01:17:08,917 --> 01:17:09,918
Malloy, talk to me!

1418
01:17:10,001 --> 01:17:11,961
Not good.
We got sparks and fire in the fuel pod.

1419
01:17:12,045 --> 01:17:14,380
<i>Independence,</i> blow those locks
and get outta there now!

1420
01:17:14,464 --> 01:17:15,840
Dump the hoses now! We're going!

1421
01:17:15,924 --> 01:17:18,218
What happened?
Let me shut off the O2 feed!

1422
01:17:18,301 --> 01:17:20,053
Harry, it's burnin' up!

1423
01:17:20,136 --> 01:17:22,639
Damn! Max, Rock, get in here!

1424
01:17:22,806 --> 01:17:24,933
Get down there
and crack these pipes over here!

1425
01:17:25,016 --> 01:17:26,392
<i>Harry, it's burnin' up!</i>

1426
01:17:26,476 --> 01:17:28,269
We're goin' back for the other team!

1427
01:17:28,353 --> 01:17:29,312
<i>[ Chatter On Radio ]</i>

1428
01:17:29,395 --> 01:17:32,065
[ Man ] Switch on
the personnel locators.

1429
01:17:32,315 --> 01:17:34,442
Trackin' A.J. He's climbin'.

1430
01:17:34,526 --> 01:17:36,402
- No!
- Go! Go!

1431
01:17:36,945 --> 01:17:40,907
It's too late! Get back to the shuttle!
This thing's gonna blow!

1432
01:17:41,407 --> 01:17:42,450
No!

1433
01:17:43,243 --> 01:17:46,830
Colonel, we gotta move now!
Come on! Close the hatch!

1434
01:17:48,748 --> 01:17:50,124
Wait a minute! Wait a minute!
We got a man in there!

1435
01:17:50,208 --> 01:17:53,169
- Open that door, and we'll all die!
- Fuel leak!

1436
01:17:53,378 --> 01:17:56,214
[ All Shouting ]

1437
01:17:56,422 --> 01:17:58,842
Evac now! Let's go! Let's go!

1438
01:18:01,094 --> 01:18:04,597
Come on back! No, wait!
The door is broken!

1439
01:18:05,849 --> 01:18:07,100
No!

1440
01:18:07,267 --> 01:18:08,852
They got the fire sealed in the fuel pod.

1441
01:18:08,935 --> 01:18:09,894
They locked it down.

1442
01:18:09,978 --> 01:18:11,062
<i>[ Man On P.A. ]
Tracking men to the shuttle.</i>

1443
01:18:11,145 --> 01:18:12,814
They've still got
two men trapped in there!

1444
01:18:14,691 --> 01:18:17,652
Keep running!
The shuttle's another 75 feet!

1445
01:18:18,111 --> 01:18:19,112
Where's the rest of the team?

1446
01:18:19,195 --> 01:18:20,196
[ All Shouting ]

1447
01:18:20,280 --> 01:18:21,364
Where's A.J.?

1448
01:18:21,447 --> 01:18:23,741
- A.J.'s gone!
- We're not leavin' without A.J.!

1449
01:18:23,825 --> 01:18:26,035
He's gone! It's too late!

1450
01:18:27,829 --> 01:18:30,456
Come on! This way is our only chance!

1451
01:18:30,665 --> 01:18:32,750
So it's minus hundred!

1452
01:18:32,834 --> 01:18:35,962
Very cold. Hold breath, or lung freezes!

1453
01:18:41,843 --> 01:18:45,805
Get back to the shuttle!
And lock that door!

1454
01:18:45,889 --> 01:18:48,141
[ All Shouting ]

1455
01:18:51,436 --> 01:18:53,229
It's on fire! It's on fire, Harry!

1456
01:18:53,313 --> 01:18:55,940
- It's them or all of us!
- It's on fire.

1457
01:18:56,065 --> 01:18:58,192
- Full thrust.
- We're gonna get hit.

1458
01:18:58,985 --> 01:19:02,822
[ Rattling, Hissing ]

1459
01:19:10,580 --> 01:19:12,874
[ Gasping ]

1460
01:19:14,584 --> 01:19:18,421
Lev! Lev, the door's gonna blow!

1461
01:19:19,589 --> 01:19:20,632
No!

1462
01:19:23,051 --> 01:19:24,302
Oh!

1463
01:19:24,719 --> 01:19:27,096
We're going! It's gonna blow!

1464
01:19:28,264 --> 01:19:29,641
A.J.'s still in there!

1465
01:19:29,724 --> 01:19:32,226
Blow the locks. No, the bolts!

1466
01:19:32,310 --> 01:19:33,811
We've gotta...

1467
01:19:33,895 --> 01:19:36,064
I think we're almost there!

1468
01:19:36,773 --> 01:19:37,857
[ All Shouting ]

1469
01:19:37,941 --> 01:19:39,442
Flight, <i>Independence</i> does not have A.J.

1470
01:19:39,525 --> 01:19:40,652
They're gonna close the door
without him.

1471
01:19:40,735 --> 01:19:42,236
<i>[ Man ] Tracking.
They're 75 feet from the shuttle.</i>

1472
01:19:42,320 --> 01:19:43,947
Just tell 'em to air lock the door and go!

1473
01:19:44,030 --> 01:19:45,365
Dog the hatch now!

1474
01:19:45,448 --> 01:19:46,449
Close it!

1475
01:19:46,532 --> 01:19:48,576
[ Explosion ]

1476
01:19:52,038 --> 01:19:52,997
Ho...

1477
01:19:53,081 --> 01:19:54,165
[ Exploding ]

1478
01:19:54,248 --> 01:19:55,541
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

1479
01:19:55,625 --> 01:19:58,711
Colonel! That thing's comin' right for...
We got to move!

1480
01:20:02,382 --> 01:20:04,133
Hurry up! There's the shuttle door!

1481
01:20:04,217 --> 01:20:05,802
[ Shouting ]

1482
01:20:06,719 --> 01:20:09,514
Fire's coming at us! Close the door now!

1483
01:20:14,602 --> 01:20:15,979
Go! Go! Go!

1484
01:20:24,278 --> 01:20:28,074
<i>Freedom,</i> the <i>Independence</i> crew
is on board and accounted for.

1485
01:20:28,533 --> 01:20:30,827
<i>We're even heavy one cosmonaut.</i>

1486
01:20:30,910 --> 01:20:32,745
They got 90 percent of their fuel.

1487
01:20:33,371 --> 01:20:34,998
Pretty intense, huh?

1488
01:20:35,081 --> 01:20:40,253
That's why I told you, "Touch nothing."
But you're bunch of cowboys.

1489
01:20:44,757 --> 01:20:47,385
<i>So while the consciousness
of the planet is unified,</i>

1490
01:20:47,468 --> 01:20:48,761
<i>focused on the NASA mission</i>

1491
01:20:48,845 --> 01:20:51,097
<i>taking place right now
in the vast ocean of space,</i>

1492
01:20:51,180 --> 01:20:52,432
<i>[ Speaking Russian ]</i>

1493
01:20:52,515 --> 01:20:54,100
<i>we're now in the final hours
of the mission,</i>

1494
01:20:54,183 --> 01:20:57,520
<i>as the</i> Freedom <i>and</i> Independence
<i>prepare to slingshot around the moon.</i>

1495
01:21:06,237 --> 01:21:09,282
Morning, guys.
It's time to suit up, I guess.

1496
01:21:09,365 --> 01:21:11,451
Uh, we got a big day.

1497
01:21:12,076 --> 01:21:13,995
Eighteen seconds to radio interrupt.

1498
01:21:14,078 --> 01:21:15,705
Booster sequence confirmed.

1499
01:21:15,788 --> 01:21:18,791
<i>This is Houston.</i>
<i>Roger that,</i> Freedom.<i> We copy.</i>

1500
01:21:19,042 --> 01:21:20,835
Shuttles are ready
for the burn around the moon.

1501
01:21:20,918 --> 01:21:23,463
Radio contact terminated. We're out.

1502
01:21:24,756 --> 01:21:28,968
Nine and a half Gs for 11 minutes.
I'd start praying about right now.

1503
01:21:34,307 --> 01:21:35,892
So this is the part
where we're supposed to just

1504
01:21:35,975 --> 01:21:38,394
hold on real tight and, uh,
hope we don't die.

1505
01:21:38,478 --> 01:21:40,480
Stand by for lunar roll.

1506
01:21:40,563 --> 01:21:42,273
High inclination. Lunar orbit.

1507
01:21:44,650 --> 01:21:47,779
You boys got those wills
filled out correctly?

1508
01:22:03,044 --> 01:22:04,921
All right, men,
this is what we trained for.

1509
01:22:05,004 --> 01:22:06,255
Now just suck it up!

1510
01:22:06,339 --> 01:22:09,383
On the mark. Five. Four.

1511
01:22:09,467 --> 01:22:11,844
Three. Two. One.

1512
01:22:22,188 --> 01:22:23,648
Is this supposed to be like this?

1513
01:22:23,731 --> 01:22:25,149
Don't worry. This is normal.

1514
01:22:25,233 --> 01:22:26,275
How would you know?

1515
01:22:26,359 --> 01:22:27,443
[ Groaning ]

1516
01:22:27,527 --> 01:22:29,362
- Fourteen thousand miles an hour.
- Four Gs.

1517
01:22:29,445 --> 01:22:31,447
- Ahh!
- How long does this last?

1518
01:22:31,531 --> 01:22:32,573
Six Gs.

1519
01:22:35,618 --> 01:22:36,661
Fifteen thousand.

1520
01:22:36,744 --> 01:22:38,746
- Really heavy, man!
- This isn't normal.

1521
01:22:38,830 --> 01:22:40,123
What do you mean, "this isn't normal"?

1522
01:22:40,206 --> 01:22:41,874
This is way worse!

1523
01:22:41,958 --> 01:22:43,709
Eight Gs. Hang tight!

1524
01:22:43,793 --> 01:22:47,797
We're not gonna make it!
Oh, we're gonna die!

1525
01:22:48,131 --> 01:22:50,591
Twelve minutes.
Flight, we still got nothin' here.

1526
01:22:50,716 --> 01:22:52,343
[ All Groaning ]

1527
01:22:52,426 --> 01:22:54,762
This is too fast!

1528
01:22:58,766 --> 01:22:59,767
Ten Gs!

1529
01:22:59,851 --> 01:23:02,061
[ Groaning Continues ]

1530
01:23:10,153 --> 01:23:11,195
[ Groaning ]

1531
01:23:11,279 --> 01:23:12,405
[ Laughing ]

1532
01:23:13,072 --> 01:23:16,576
[ Sharp ] We're maxed at 22,500!

1533
01:23:17,952 --> 01:23:20,204
[ Groaning ]

1534
01:23:21,747 --> 01:23:23,541
[ Rattling Ceases ]

1535
01:23:23,624 --> 01:23:24,709
[ Exhales ]

1536
01:23:26,627 --> 01:23:29,422
<i>We have acquisition of signal
from</i> Independence <i>and</i> Freedom.

1537
01:23:29,505 --> 01:23:30,506
[ Relieved Chattering ]

1538
01:23:30,590 --> 01:23:33,342
We're in, guys.
All right. Welcome back, team.

1539
01:23:33,551 --> 01:23:36,179
We have visual of the target, Houston.

1540
01:23:45,188 --> 01:23:46,731
You see that?

1541
01:23:51,444 --> 01:23:52,528
Wow.

1542
01:23:54,322 --> 01:23:55,573
[ Computer Blipping ]

1543
01:23:55,656 --> 01:23:57,158
Come in, <i>Independence.</i>

1544
01:23:57,241 --> 01:23:59,994
<i>[ Sharp] Houston, you gotta see this
to believe it.</i>

1545
01:24:02,163 --> 01:24:03,748
Okay, team, let's take 'em in.

1546
01:24:03,831 --> 01:24:05,625
Okay, Quincy, how much tail debris
do we have?

1547
01:24:05,708 --> 01:24:07,877
<i>[ Man ]</i> Freedom, <i>turn on FOD radar.</i>

1548
01:24:07,960 --> 01:24:09,045
FOD radar on.

1549
01:24:09,128 --> 01:24:10,338
[ Blipping ]

1550
01:24:11,672 --> 01:24:13,883
Everybody, hang on.
This could get a little rough.

1551
01:24:13,966 --> 01:24:15,885
Engaging evasive radar.

1552
01:24:23,476 --> 01:24:24,727
Hold on!

1553
01:24:36,113 --> 01:24:37,990
Goddamn! We got debris!

1554
01:24:39,992 --> 01:24:42,703
<i>[ Watts]
We're dumping auxiliary boosters.</i>

1555
01:24:55,716 --> 01:24:58,511
<i>- Houston, do you read me?
- We got debris!</i>

1556
01:25:01,013 --> 01:25:02,765
We're goin' in! We're comin' in hot!

1557
01:25:07,186 --> 01:25:08,854
Independence, <i>try to maintain
your present heading.</i>

1558
01:25:08,938 --> 01:25:10,022
<i>You've got a target L.Z.</i>

1559
01:25:10,106 --> 01:25:12,316
There's too much debris!
We gotta peel off!

1560
01:25:12,400 --> 01:25:13,693
Negative!

1561
01:25:14,110 --> 01:25:16,404
[ Loud Crashing ]

1562
01:25:16,988 --> 01:25:18,322
We're hit!

1563
01:25:20,783 --> 01:25:21,993
<i>Mayday, mayday!</i>

1564
01:25:22,076 --> 01:25:23,953
I've lost main thrusters.
Get 'em back up!

1565
01:25:24,036 --> 01:25:26,372
Mayday, Houston, mayday!
We've lost R.C.S. thrusters!

1566
01:25:26,455 --> 01:25:28,165
<i>Mayday,</i> Freedom, <i>mayday!</i>

1567
01:25:28,249 --> 01:25:30,418
We are out of control!
We are going down!

1568
01:25:30,501 --> 01:25:32,753
Do you read me?
<i>Freedom,</i> we are going down!

1569
01:25:42,346 --> 01:25:43,347
[ All Shouting ]

1570
01:25:43,431 --> 01:25:45,516
[ Thrusters Roaring ]

1571
01:25:46,183 --> 01:25:47,143
We're gonna hit!

1572
01:25:47,226 --> 01:25:48,311
[ Blipping ]

1573
01:25:57,695 --> 01:26:02,074
Everybody, go to your own life support!
Lock yourself in the cargo bay!

1574
01:26:03,951 --> 01:26:05,328
We are going down!

1575
01:26:05,411 --> 01:26:09,123
Houston! Houston, we are going down!
We have lost control!

1576
01:26:09,206 --> 01:26:10,875
I can't get it on!

1577
01:26:13,127 --> 01:26:14,628
Good luck, <i>Freedom.</i>

1578
01:26:14,712 --> 01:26:16,714
Oh, my God, this is it.

1579
01:26:18,758 --> 01:26:20,009
[ Blipping ]

1580
01:26:20,092 --> 01:26:22,928
[ All Screaming ]

1581
01:26:33,064 --> 01:26:35,858
[ Lev Shouting In Russian ]

1582
01:26:54,794 --> 01:26:56,128
[ Screams ]

1583
01:27:07,181 --> 01:27:10,643
Sharp, what the hell is that?
Is that the <i>Independence?</i>

1584
01:27:15,481 --> 01:27:17,566
<i>[ Sharp] Houston,</i> Independence
<i>is a dead stick.</i>

1585
01:27:17,650 --> 01:27:19,902
<i>They're not gonna make it.</i>

1586
01:27:31,664 --> 01:27:34,208
<i>Houston,</i>
Independence <i>has gone down.</i>

1587
01:27:46,303 --> 01:27:48,639
When I touch this baby down,
full reverse thrust.

1588
01:27:48,722 --> 01:27:50,724
- Fires on your right, Sharp!
- Reversing the thrusters!

1589
01:27:50,808 --> 01:27:52,852
[ Thrusters Roaring ]

1590
01:27:52,935 --> 01:27:54,854
Hang tight! Hang tight!

1591
01:27:55,855 --> 01:27:59,233
Houston, we overshot our landing field.
We overshot our landing field.

1592
01:27:59,316 --> 01:28:01,235
Oh, no!

1593
01:28:06,365 --> 01:28:07,366
[ Grunting ]

1594
01:28:08,617 --> 01:28:10,369
[ Ice Smashing ]

1595
01:28:14,498 --> 01:28:15,916
[ Shouting ]

1596
01:28:21,464 --> 01:28:22,840
- God!
- Aah!

1597
01:28:25,593 --> 01:28:26,635
[ Crashing Stops ]

1598
01:28:26,719 --> 01:28:29,680
[ Whimpering, Panting ]

1599
01:28:32,099 --> 01:28:34,059
[ Whimpering ]

1600
01:28:34,143 --> 01:28:36,103
[ Panting ]

1601
01:28:38,981 --> 01:28:42,735
Initiate system light system check.
Make sure we can still get off this rock.

1602
01:28:42,818 --> 01:28:45,279
Our electrical system is screwed.
I'm going to back-up.

1603
01:28:45,362 --> 01:28:47,156
Fuel seals check. Engine seals check.

1604
01:28:47,239 --> 01:28:50,075
- Oh, God. Oh!
- Pressure seals check.

1605
01:28:53,412 --> 01:28:54,413
Anyone hurt?

1606
01:28:54,497 --> 01:28:56,916
[ Panting ] Where's...

1607
01:28:58,459 --> 01:29:02,129
Where's the other shuttle?
What happened to the other shuttle?

1608
01:29:02,213 --> 01:29:04,423
<i>Independence</i> is off the grid.

1609
01:29:04,715 --> 01:29:05,716
"Off the grid"?

1610
01:29:05,799 --> 01:29:09,011
What are you, a freakin' cyborg?
What does that mean?

1611
01:29:09,094 --> 01:29:11,472
Hey, you saw it yourself, right?

1612
01:29:11,805 --> 01:29:13,265
They're gone.

1613
01:29:14,683 --> 01:29:18,187
Come in, <i>Freedom.</i> This is
CAPCOM Houston.<i> Freedom,</i> come in.

1614
01:29:18,270 --> 01:29:21,106
This is CAPCOM Houston.
Come in, <i>Freedom.</i>

1615
01:29:22,316 --> 01:29:23,859
- God!
- Let's just ask God

1616
01:29:23,943 --> 01:29:25,903
to take care of our friends.

1617
01:29:27,738 --> 01:29:29,615
May they rest in peace.

1618
01:29:30,991 --> 01:29:32,117
Amen.

1619
01:29:32,493 --> 01:29:34,537
[ Computers Blipping ]

1620
01:29:40,251 --> 01:29:41,961
We got eight hours.

1621
01:29:42,378 --> 01:29:43,379
[ Gasps ]

1622
01:29:43,462 --> 01:29:46,090
Let's get this job done and go home.

1623
01:29:46,549 --> 01:29:47,550
Nothin'.

1624
01:29:47,633 --> 01:29:50,010
Come on, Watts, Sharp, somebody.

1625
01:29:50,469 --> 01:29:52,471
This is CAPCOM Houston.

1626
01:29:53,973 --> 01:29:57,768
Come in, <i>Freedom. Freedom,</i> come in.
This is CAPCOM Houston.

1627
01:29:59,728 --> 01:30:01,814
Maybe you shouldn't be here.

1628
01:30:01,897 --> 01:30:04,233
I don't have anywhere else to go.

1629
01:30:04,316 --> 01:30:06,151
<i>Freedom,</i> come in.
This is CAPCOM Houston.

1630
01:30:08,320 --> 01:30:11,031
All right, let's get the tools unpacked
and fire up the Armadillo.

1631
01:30:11,115 --> 01:30:13,325
We're not getting a damn thing
on the inertial nav system.

1632
01:30:13,409 --> 01:30:15,911
- I know where we are.
- Please step away.

1633
01:30:15,995 --> 01:30:17,329
Radio signal's dead.

1634
01:30:17,413 --> 01:30:19,081
I'm flipping the backup generator.

1635
01:30:19,164 --> 01:30:21,667
Radio signal's gonna be cut in half
till we get main power back.

1636
01:30:21,750 --> 01:30:27,256
We're in segment 202, lateral grid 9,
site 15H-32, give or take a few yards.

1637
01:30:27,339 --> 01:30:30,926
Captain America here
blew the landing by 26 miles.

1638
01:30:31,010 --> 01:30:33,262
How the hell do you know that?

1639
01:30:33,345 --> 01:30:35,097
Because I'm a genius.

1640
01:30:35,180 --> 01:30:36,181
The gauges will not read.

1641
01:30:36,265 --> 01:30:38,642
They're all peaked, like we're plugged
into some magnetic field.

1642
01:30:38,726 --> 01:30:40,519
Well, who on this spaceship
wants to know why?

1643
01:30:40,603 --> 01:30:43,063
- [ Sharp ] By all means.
- The reason we were shooting for grid 8

1644
01:30:43,147 --> 01:30:47,818
is because thermographics indicated
that grid 9 was compressed iron ferrite.

1645
01:30:48,986 --> 01:30:52,531
Which means that you landed us
on a goddamn iron plate.

1646
01:30:55,200 --> 01:30:56,160
All right. Well, you heard the man.

1647
01:30:56,243 --> 01:30:58,162
Let's wheel out the remote satellite link.
We need that radio.

1648
01:30:58,245 --> 01:30:59,872
Oh, God, please tell me
we still got one of 'em.

1649
01:30:59,955 --> 01:31:02,041
[ Computers Beeping ]

1650
01:31:03,000 --> 01:31:04,668
[ Man ] <i>Independence</i> has flat-lined.

1651
01:31:05,294 --> 01:31:06,795
[ Weeping ]

1652
01:31:34,531 --> 01:31:37,242
[ Sighs, Grunting ]

1653
01:31:45,751 --> 01:31:48,128
Oh. Oh.

1654
01:31:49,755 --> 01:31:51,924
Oscar! Oscar!

1655
01:31:54,343 --> 01:31:56,095
Oh, God!

1656
01:31:59,598 --> 01:32:03,102
Hello! Anyone! Is anyone else alive?

1657
01:32:04,186 --> 01:32:05,979
Somebody, help me!

1658
01:32:07,981 --> 01:32:09,191
A.J.!

1659
01:32:10,693 --> 01:32:12,319
Where are you?

1660
01:32:12,403 --> 01:32:13,737
I'm here.

1661
01:32:14,655 --> 01:32:16,073
[ Grunting ]

1662
01:32:18,325 --> 01:32:20,536
Lev, there's no one else.

1663
01:32:21,495 --> 01:32:22,830
There's no one else.

1664
01:32:22,913 --> 01:32:24,248
I know.

1665
01:32:24,498 --> 01:32:26,208
[ Bear ] Oh, man.

1666
01:32:26,917 --> 01:32:29,837
[ A.J. I Bear, where are you?
[ Bear ] A.J.? A.J.?

1667
01:32:31,672 --> 01:32:33,757
[ Bear ] I'm in the shuttle, man.

1668
01:32:33,841 --> 01:32:34,842
[ Grunts ]

1669
01:32:34,925 --> 01:32:36,635
Are you all right?

1670
01:32:36,969 --> 01:32:39,138
I'm so glad to see you, man.

1671
01:32:39,430 --> 01:32:42,474
I never thought I'd be so happy
to see your ugly face.

1672
01:32:42,808 --> 01:32:45,144
Houston, do you read? This is <i>Freedom.</i>

1673
01:32:45,227 --> 01:32:46,520
<i>[ Sharp] Check your thrusters.</i>

1674
01:32:46,603 --> 01:32:48,313
[ Watts ] Houston, do you copy?

1675
01:32:48,397 --> 01:32:49,982
[ Sharp ] Is everyone good to go?

1676
01:33:00,993 --> 01:33:02,161
Wow.

1677
01:33:12,796 --> 01:33:15,215
[ Harry ] Down here! In the valley!

1678
01:33:16,175 --> 01:33:19,178
This place is like
Dr. Seuss's worst nightmare.

1679
01:33:19,261 --> 01:33:22,723
Let's get the remote satellite.
We'll get better reception up there.

1680
01:33:24,016 --> 01:33:25,601
[ Harry ] Bring Max down.

1681
01:33:25,684 --> 01:33:29,062
Watch yourself through here, Max.
There're a couple big fissures.

1682
01:33:29,146 --> 01:33:30,397
To the left!

1683
01:33:30,481 --> 01:33:32,441
Bring it to the left!

1684
01:33:37,696 --> 01:33:39,031
[ Harry ] Rockhound,
you come on down here

1685
01:33:39,114 --> 01:33:41,700
and take some readings
down in the flat spot.

1686
01:33:41,784 --> 01:33:43,994
[ Beeping ]

1687
01:33:44,077 --> 01:33:45,621
Iron ferrite.

1688
01:33:48,749 --> 01:33:50,250
I have fire.

1689
01:33:50,334 --> 01:33:53,128
[ Harry ] Watts, I'm comin' back.
Stand by.

1690
01:33:53,212 --> 01:33:55,088
Mostly iron, Rockhound.

1691
01:33:55,547 --> 01:33:57,257
God, I hate knowing everything.

1692
01:33:57,341 --> 01:34:00,052
We couldn't have picked
a worse spot to drill.

1693
01:34:00,135 --> 01:34:04,223
Well, I can pretty much guarantee
it's not gonna be thicker than 50 feet.

1694
01:34:04,306 --> 01:34:07,434
- How do you figure that?
- 'Cause if it is, we're screwed.

1695
01:34:09,478 --> 01:34:12,147
- Max, you good?
- Yeah. Just makin' hole.

1696
01:34:12,231 --> 01:34:13,607
Turn it around.

1697
01:34:13,690 --> 01:34:15,776
[ Max ] Friggin' outer space.

1698
01:34:18,237 --> 01:34:19,613
It's good.

1699
01:34:26,662 --> 01:34:30,290
All right. We're in. Another light.
We're cuttin' through pretty good.

1700
01:34:30,374 --> 01:34:33,460
There's some stuff in here
I ain't never seen.

1701
01:34:33,794 --> 01:34:35,712
All right, let's punch it down!

1702
01:34:35,796 --> 01:34:37,381
[ Metal Creaking ]

1703
01:34:37,464 --> 01:34:40,175
- Hey, Harry, did you see that?
- Yeah, Max, I see it. I see it. What is it?

1704
01:34:40,259 --> 01:34:41,510
We lost the bite in the bit.

1705
01:34:41,593 --> 01:34:43,846
All right. Back it off. Back it off.

1706
01:34:43,929 --> 01:34:45,305
Goddamn it!

1707
01:34:45,389 --> 01:34:47,558
Sounds like we twisted a shank.
Back it out of there, Max.

1708
01:34:47,641 --> 01:34:49,768
Good. Good. Hold 'er there.

1709
01:34:54,064 --> 01:34:57,025
Wow, this is a goddamn Greek tragedy.

1710
01:34:57,359 --> 01:34:59,528
We've all seen
broken drill heads before.

1711
01:34:59,611 --> 01:35:01,363
Not after ten feet.

1712
01:35:01,446 --> 01:35:04,199
- I never seen one.
- Well, now you've seen one.

1713
01:35:04,283 --> 01:35:06,785
- What do you want?
- Unpack the Judge.

1714
01:35:09,288 --> 01:35:10,914
[ A.J. I Bear, Lev.

1715
01:35:11,790 --> 01:35:14,918
[ Lev ] We're only
three astronauts left now.

1716
01:35:15,502 --> 01:35:17,212
[ A.J. I We're not astronauts.
We're oil drillers.

1717
01:35:17,296 --> 01:35:19,298
We're not even supposed to be here.

1718
01:35:19,381 --> 01:35:21,466
What? You're not astronaut?

1719
01:35:22,009 --> 01:35:24,803
- I'm getting us outta here. Get in.
- Why?

1720
01:35:24,887 --> 01:35:27,264
Just get in the Armadillo. I have an idea.

1721
01:35:27,347 --> 01:35:29,433
Houston, this is <i>Freedom.</i> Do you copy?

1722
01:35:29,516 --> 01:35:32,060
Houston, do you copy?
<i>Freedom</i> shuttle has...

1723
01:35:32,144 --> 01:35:33,770
<i>[ Radio Static Hissing]</i>

1724
01:35:33,854 --> 01:35:36,523
We're gettin'
some scattered video feeds here.

1725
01:35:36,607 --> 01:35:38,734
<i>[ Watts] Houston, this is</i> Freedom.
<i>Do you copy?</i>

1726
01:35:38,817 --> 01:35:41,403
- Thank God we have you, <i>Freedom.</i>
<i>- Freedom,</i> this is Houston. Go ahead.

1727
01:35:41,486 --> 01:35:43,989
- Don't lose 'em, Malloy.
<i>- Sharp, I'm getting something.</i>

1728
01:35:44,072 --> 01:35:45,073
<i>Houston, this is</i> Freedom.

1729
01:35:45,157 --> 01:35:46,950
<i>- We have landed safely.</i>
- Where are they?

1730
01:35:47,034 --> 01:35:49,745
<i>We are at site coordinates
approximately 15H-32...</i>

1731
01:35:49,828 --> 01:35:51,580
Okay, I want to know everything
we can about that location.

1732
01:35:51,663 --> 01:35:52,831
- Got it.
- Get it before we lose 'em.

1733
01:35:52,915 --> 01:35:55,083
<i>We're also having electric
and antenna difficulties.</i>

1734
01:35:55,167 --> 01:35:56,418
Walter, get Mechanical on that.

1735
01:35:56,501 --> 01:35:58,462
<i>But we have commenced drilling.</i>

1736
01:35:58,545 --> 01:36:00,464
Stevens, we're losin' him.
Bring it up on four. On four.

1737
01:36:00,547 --> 01:36:03,842
- Come on.
<i>- Shuttle flight capability not yet known.</i>

1738
01:36:04,217 --> 01:36:05,218
- Bump the signal.
- Bumping.

1739
01:36:05,302 --> 01:36:06,595
Houston. Houston.

1740
01:36:06,678 --> 01:36:09,222
We lost 'em. Get 'em back.
Gruber, we need that hookup.

1741
01:36:11,767 --> 01:36:13,977
Show you how we do things
where I come from.

1742
01:36:22,194 --> 01:36:23,528
Hold on!

1743
01:36:25,447 --> 01:36:27,532
[ Metal Crumpling ]

1744
01:36:33,330 --> 01:36:34,706
Seat it.

1745
01:36:35,374 --> 01:36:38,085
All right, get ready. Max, thread it.

1746
01:36:39,544 --> 01:36:42,673
Guys, the clock is tickin'.
Let's go, go, go, go, go!

1747
01:36:42,756 --> 01:36:44,841
All right! Good! Crank it loose!

1748
01:36:44,925 --> 01:36:48,011
Keep it at 25.
Let's kick a little asteroid butt!

1749
01:36:48,095 --> 01:36:50,305
All right, Chick. Give me more torque
on the turbine, huh?

1750
01:36:50,389 --> 01:36:51,640
[ Drill Whining ]

1751
01:36:51,723 --> 01:36:53,141
[ Harry ] Max, I need some more power
down here!

1752
01:36:53,225 --> 01:36:54,559
- All right, boss.
- Throw it in fourth,

1753
01:36:54,643 --> 01:36:55,811
then drop the hammer.

1754
01:36:55,894 --> 01:36:57,479
Let's drill through this turd.

1755
01:36:57,562 --> 01:36:59,982
[ Harry ] Come on, boys.
We gotta hop. We're fallin' behind.

1756
01:37:00,065 --> 01:37:02,985
Dig, dig, dig. Chew this iron bitch up.

1757
01:37:03,902 --> 01:37:06,029
[ Metal Whining ]

1758
01:37:08,281 --> 01:37:09,992
- Chick, the tranny's stuck.
- Harry!

1759
01:37:10,075 --> 01:37:11,451
What is it?

1760
01:37:12,077 --> 01:37:13,078
Chick, come on! Help!

1761
01:37:13,161 --> 01:37:14,830
- Release the clutch!
- Pull it up!

1762
01:37:14,913 --> 01:37:17,457
Okay. Well, this thing's not movin'.

1763
01:37:18,458 --> 01:37:21,086
No, no, no! Shut it down! Shut it...

1764
01:37:22,546 --> 01:37:24,756
[ Groaning ]

1765
01:37:28,385 --> 01:37:30,345
This is not workin' out, Harry.

1766
01:37:30,429 --> 01:37:34,516
- Oh, are you all right?
- Oh, blew the tranny. Blew the tranny.

1767
01:37:35,809 --> 01:37:37,269
Come on, God.

1768
01:37:38,687 --> 01:37:41,815
Just a little help. That's all I'm askin'.

1769
01:37:42,482 --> 01:37:45,652
I think we're close enough.
He might've heard ya.

1770
01:37:48,530 --> 01:37:50,866
Here's the bad news.
Before the asteroid passed the moon,

1771
01:37:50,949 --> 01:37:54,202
her rotation was stable
at 32 degrees on an x axis.

1772
01:37:54,286 --> 01:37:58,206
But now look at this.
The lunar gravity's put her in a spin.

1773
01:37:58,540 --> 01:38:02,002
She's tumbling on all three axes.
This wasn't expected, sir.

1774
01:38:02,085 --> 01:38:04,671
- What does this do for communications?
- Not good.

1775
01:38:04,755 --> 01:38:07,424
We'll have definite contact with
the shuttle for only seven more minutes.

1776
01:38:07,507 --> 01:38:10,302
- After that it's radio darkness.
- For how long?

1777
01:38:10,385 --> 01:38:14,139
And after seven minutes,
we may never hear from them again.

1778
01:38:14,598 --> 01:38:16,099
But we're trying to bounce a signal

1779
01:38:16,183 --> 01:38:18,643
off a Russian military satellite,
reestablish contact that way.

1780
01:38:18,727 --> 01:38:20,562
If we lose the shuttle com,

1781
01:38:20,645 --> 01:38:23,190
when do we lose the ability
to remote detonate that nuke?

1782
01:38:23,273 --> 01:38:25,692
The weapon remote receives a signal
from a Milstar satellite.

1783
01:38:25,776 --> 01:38:27,778
Higher orbit, more powerful transmitter.

1784
01:38:27,861 --> 01:38:29,780
If we've got the shuttle
for seven minutes,

1785
01:38:29,863 --> 01:38:32,199
we can remote detonate
for an additional five.

1786
01:38:32,282 --> 01:38:34,409
What he's trying to say, General,
is that, uh, in 12 minutes' time,

1787
01:38:34,493 --> 01:38:38,121
you may lose the ability
to detonate the nuke... permanently.

1788
01:38:38,205 --> 01:38:40,040
I've got to inform the president.

1789
01:38:41,666 --> 01:38:44,252
Just want to make sure you know
we're stuck on an asteroid.

1790
01:38:44,336 --> 01:38:46,254
- Do you know what you're doing now?
- No, no.

1791
01:38:46,338 --> 01:38:49,633
You know what? I have no idea
what I'm doing. I have no idea.

1792
01:38:49,716 --> 01:38:52,010
This button,
I don't know what that does, okay?

1793
01:38:52,094 --> 01:38:54,638
All I know is
that we just crashed back there,

1794
01:38:54,721 --> 01:38:57,599
I lost two of my friends,
we're 25 miles from Harry's shuttle.

1795
01:38:57,682 --> 01:39:00,102
We don't know if he's alive.
We don't know if he can fly.

1796
01:39:00,185 --> 01:39:01,895
All I know is,
there's a beep on this thing

1797
01:39:01,978 --> 01:39:03,105
and I'm trying to get us there.

1798
01:39:10,779 --> 01:39:11,780
[ Beeping ]

1799
01:39:11,863 --> 01:39:13,865
Let's get it unpacked.

1800
01:39:14,991 --> 01:39:15,951
What's up?

1801
01:39:16,034 --> 01:39:18,745
We're drilling through some
kind of metal I've never seen before.

1802
01:39:18,829 --> 01:39:21,790
It's fried two of our drill bits,
and now we blew our first transmission.

1803
01:39:21,873 --> 01:39:22,874
So how deep are we?

1804
01:39:22,958 --> 01:39:24,668
We could use your help
with the transmission, Colonel.

1805
01:39:24,751 --> 01:39:27,629
I have an assessment report due now.
We're supposed to be at 200 feet.

1806
01:39:27,712 --> 01:39:30,465
- So how deep are we?
- Not as deep as we'll be

1807
01:39:30,549 --> 01:39:32,050
when you quit askin' me
these questions

1808
01:39:32,134 --> 01:39:33,718
and help us load this transmission on.

1809
01:39:33,802 --> 01:39:35,053
What is our current depth?

1810
01:39:35,137 --> 01:39:36,930
Our current depth
is not important, Colonel.

1811
01:39:37,013 --> 01:39:40,058
I'll decide what's important.
We've got 800 feet to drill.

1812
01:39:40,142 --> 01:39:43,145
You've had two and a half hours.
Where are we?

1813
01:39:44,855 --> 01:39:46,439
We're at 57 feet.

1814
01:39:47,065 --> 01:39:48,066
Now, if you're not too busy,

1815
01:39:48,150 --> 01:39:50,443
maybe you can give us a hand
with this transmission.

1816
01:39:50,527 --> 01:39:52,070
Colonel Sharp!

1817
01:39:53,196 --> 01:39:55,907
Get this strapped up. I'll be right back.
Colonel Sharp!

1818
01:39:55,991 --> 01:39:59,202
<i>All right. I'm coming through.
We have contact. Over.</i>

1819
01:39:59,286 --> 01:40:01,872
That's as clear as it's gonna get.

1820
01:40:02,622 --> 01:40:04,833
Houston, this is <i>Freedom.</i> Do you copy?

1821
01:40:04,916 --> 01:40:07,502
<i>Working at a remote satellite link
at this moment.</i>

1822
01:40:07,586 --> 01:40:08,837
<i>- Transmission change.</i>
- Colonel!

1823
01:40:08,920 --> 01:40:11,590
Twenty minutes.
Puts drilling final at ten hours.

1824
01:40:11,673 --> 01:40:15,177
Please advise. That's four hours
past the zero barrier. Please advise.

1825
01:40:15,260 --> 01:40:18,054
What the hell is this? "Zero depth"?

1826
01:40:18,263 --> 01:40:21,016
And where'd this come from?
Who are you talkin' to? Is that Truman?

1827
01:40:21,099 --> 01:40:22,517
Lemme have that phone.
Gimme the phone.

1828
01:40:22,601 --> 01:40:25,562
Truman! Look, this is what happens
when you drill.

1829
01:40:25,645 --> 01:40:29,900
We cannot use your "U.S. Air Force
Personnel Only" drill time card.

1830
01:40:29,983 --> 01:40:32,110
- Who wrote this thing, by the way?
- We're losing come again.

1831
01:40:32,194 --> 01:40:34,404
Look. Is he getting this?
Does he hear me or...

1832
01:40:34,487 --> 01:40:35,822
<i>- What's wrong with this?
- The com's down.</i>

1833
01:40:35,906 --> 01:40:36,865
<i>What do you mean, "the com's down"?</i>

1834
01:40:36,948 --> 01:40:38,283
<i>[ Sharp] What do I mean?
I mean we've lost</i>

1835
01:40:38,366 --> 01:40:39,910
<i>- communication to mission control.</i>
- Fine.

1836
01:40:39,993 --> 01:40:41,953
Let's go back to the cargo bay
and get the transmission...

1837
01:40:42,037 --> 01:40:45,373
Harry, guess what. You had your shot.
You didn't do it. You understand me?

1838
01:40:45,457 --> 01:40:47,209
<i>- You can't...
- Why don't you stay here...</i>

1839
01:40:47,292 --> 01:40:49,252
<i>[ Shouting]</i>

1840
01:40:50,045 --> 01:40:52,005
<i>Write a report, why don't ya?
That'll be...</i>

1841
01:40:52,088 --> 01:40:53,673
<i>[ Shouting Continues]</i>

1842
01:40:53,798 --> 01:40:55,967
My men and I will go
and get this hole dug!

1843
01:40:56,051 --> 01:41:00,055
You and your men are the biggest
mistake in the history of NASA.

1844
01:41:02,432 --> 01:41:05,435
<i>- [ Man ] We've lost communication.</i>
- Oh, God.

1845
01:41:07,979 --> 01:41:12,192
- We're not lookin' too good right now.
- No shit.

1846
01:41:13,235 --> 01:41:14,945
We gotta get that radio back up.

1847
01:41:17,322 --> 01:41:20,533
[ Man ] Mr. President,
it's time to make a decision.

1848
01:41:20,617 --> 01:41:24,913
We can remote detonate the bomb
for only another five minutes.

1849
01:41:25,163 --> 01:41:26,539
[ Rings ]

1850
01:41:26,831 --> 01:41:29,668
Yes? Kimsey here. Yes, Mr. President.

1851
01:41:30,961 --> 01:41:33,004
Yes, we saw that, too, sir.

1852
01:41:33,672 --> 01:41:36,341
But maybe we should wait until they...

1853
01:41:42,764 --> 01:41:45,976
Dan, get them out of there.

1854
01:41:46,810 --> 01:41:49,187
- Evac right now.
- What's goin' on here?

1855
01:41:49,271 --> 01:41:51,106
I've been ordered
to override the system.

1856
01:41:51,189 --> 01:41:53,400
[ Elevator Bells Dinging ]

1857
01:41:56,069 --> 01:41:58,029
Well, what is this?

1858
01:42:02,492 --> 01:42:04,244
Secondary protocol.

1859
01:42:10,500 --> 01:42:13,128
But they haven't drilled
the damn hole yet!

1860
01:42:17,382 --> 01:42:19,551
The president's advisors feel
that the drilling isn't working.

1861
01:42:19,634 --> 01:42:21,511
And we've lost radio contact,
maybe for good.

1862
01:42:21,594 --> 01:42:22,637
We've only got a few minutes left of

1863
01:42:22,721 --> 01:42:24,848
guaranteed ability to
remote detonate that nuke.

1864
01:42:24,931 --> 01:42:27,434
If we don't do it now we could lose
control, and we may never get it back.

1865
01:42:27,517 --> 01:42:30,729
Well, you tell the president that
he better fire his so-called advisors.

1866
01:42:30,812 --> 01:42:32,314
If you detonate that nuke on the surface,

1867
01:42:32,397 --> 01:42:34,107
we waste a perfectly good bomb,

1868
01:42:34,190 --> 01:42:36,026
and we have one chance
to save this planet!

1869
01:42:36,109 --> 01:42:37,610
[ Beeping ]

1870
01:42:47,078 --> 01:42:48,621
I need that radio.

1871
01:42:49,122 --> 01:42:51,333
<i>Gruber, give me
everything you got now!</i>

1872
01:42:51,416 --> 01:42:52,459
<i>[ Gruber] Roger that.</i>

1873
01:42:55,795 --> 01:42:57,505
Yes, Mr. President,
I understand that completely,

1874
01:42:57,589 --> 01:42:59,632
but my point is very, very simple.

1875
01:42:59,716 --> 01:43:02,260
And I think you need to trust me on this
because I know something about it.

1876
01:43:02,344 --> 01:43:05,972
I guarantee you,
if you do this, you kill us all.

1877
01:43:09,351 --> 01:43:10,769
Yes, sir.

1878
01:43:11,269 --> 01:43:14,022
General, he wants you.

1879
01:43:15,899 --> 01:43:18,151
This is Kimsey. Yes, sir.

1880
01:43:19,277 --> 01:43:20,737
I understand.

1881
01:43:23,656 --> 01:43:27,327
The orders are to remote detonate
in 30 seconds.

1882
01:43:27,410 --> 01:43:32,540
You have not told them yet!
That is my father up there!

1883
01:43:32,624 --> 01:43:35,960
This is one order you shouldn't follow,
and you fucking know it!

1884
01:43:36,044 --> 01:43:38,004
Let her go. Let her go!

1885
01:43:40,965 --> 01:43:42,467
Your key, sir.

1886
01:43:44,928 --> 01:43:46,596
[ Consoles Beeping ]

1887
01:43:47,597 --> 01:43:49,307
God be with them.

1888
01:43:50,433 --> 01:43:52,060
Slow it down.

1889
01:43:52,310 --> 01:43:53,686
[ Beeping ]

1890
01:43:54,979 --> 01:43:56,523
[ Timer Beeping ]

1891
01:43:58,650 --> 01:43:59,943
Harry,

1892
01:44:00,652 --> 01:44:04,114
the clock on that nine-foot
nuclear weapon is ticking.

1893
01:44:05,657 --> 01:44:09,828
Oh, my God! Sharp! Get back here now!

1894
01:44:10,495 --> 01:44:12,580
What?
Get the shuttle ready to evac now!

1895
01:44:12,664 --> 01:44:13,915
It just came on all by itself.

1896
01:44:13,998 --> 01:44:15,542
- What the hell's happening?
- Secondary protocol.

1897
01:44:15,625 --> 01:44:17,544
- What's that? What?
- Secondary protocol.

1898
01:44:17,627 --> 01:44:19,170
- What does that mean?
- What the hell's secondary protocol?

1899
01:44:19,254 --> 01:44:20,463
They're detonating this thing from Earth.

1900
01:44:20,547 --> 01:44:21,589
- What do you mean, detonating?
- We haven't even

1901
01:44:21,673 --> 01:44:22,882
- drilled the hole yet!
- We'll drop it in the hole.

1902
01:44:22,966 --> 01:44:24,134
- What're you talkin' about?
- The hole? Whoa, whoa!

1903
01:44:24,217 --> 01:44:25,301
Get your helmets on now!

1904
01:44:25,385 --> 01:44:28,388
- Oh, no, no. How... How you turn it off?
- I got two men out on that rock!

1905
01:44:28,471 --> 01:44:30,723
I got a man out there, too.
We gotta evac now.

1906
01:44:30,807 --> 01:44:32,767
Max, Rockhound,
get back to the shuttle, double-time!

1907
01:44:32,851 --> 01:44:35,770
- They could be on their way here.
- They're not on their way here.

1908
01:44:35,854 --> 01:44:38,606
They would've talked to us by now.
We would've seen them.

1909
01:44:38,690 --> 01:44:41,901
- Watts, air lock the cockpit now!
- I copy you.

1910
01:44:41,985 --> 01:44:43,820
- Max, Rockhound!
- Hey, wait a minute!

1911
01:44:43,903 --> 01:44:45,280
How do you turn this thing off?

1912
01:44:45,363 --> 01:44:46,573
<i>[ Radio Static Hissing]</i>

1913
01:44:46,656 --> 01:44:48,700
- Harry, do you copy?
- Something's wrong.

1914
01:44:48,783 --> 01:44:51,619
Yeah, it's all wrong, man.
We shouldn't even be up here.

1915
01:44:51,703 --> 01:44:53,621
I know. Let's go back to the ship!

1916
01:44:54,873 --> 01:44:56,583
I'm not leavin' without my men, Sharp.

1917
01:44:56,666 --> 01:44:59,419
We've got two and a half minutes
to drop it and get off this rock.

1918
01:44:59,502 --> 01:45:01,963
If they're not back by the time we finish,
we leave without 'em.

1919
01:45:02,046 --> 01:45:04,466
Okay, let's simplify this.
Let's just turn the bomb off right now.

1920
01:45:04,549 --> 01:45:07,510
If we don't put this bomb down
in a hole 800 feet onto a fault line,

1921
01:45:07,594 --> 01:45:09,721
all you're gonna have is
a real expensive fireworks show.

1922
01:45:09,804 --> 01:45:12,265
This is turnin' into a
surrealistic nightmare here.

1923
01:45:12,682 --> 01:45:14,976
Watsler, are you listening? It's Truman.

1924
01:45:15,059 --> 01:45:18,897
Okay, listen to me carefully.
I want you to kill it. Kill the uplink.

1925
01:45:30,408 --> 01:45:32,911
Give us the time, Sharp.
Shut this bomb down now!

1926
01:45:32,994 --> 01:45:34,579
- It's not my call.
- Then whose call is it?

1927
01:45:34,662 --> 01:45:36,664
An order to detonate can
only come from the president.

1928
01:45:36,748 --> 01:45:38,291
- The president's not here!
- Let's just turn it off now.

1929
01:45:38,374 --> 01:45:39,501
You've gotta give us more time!

1930
01:45:39,584 --> 01:45:40,835
I'm telling you to
shut this bomb down now!

1931
01:45:40,919 --> 01:45:42,504
And I'm telling you it's not my call!

1932
01:45:42,587 --> 01:45:44,506
Well, guess what.
I just made the call for you.

1933
01:45:44,589 --> 01:45:45,798
Harry!

1934
01:45:47,926 --> 01:45:51,012
Don't. You could set it off.

1935
01:45:51,095 --> 01:45:54,682
Oh, man.
What're you doin' with a gun in space?

1936
01:45:57,769 --> 01:46:01,147
Come on, come on.
We gotta stop that bomb right now.

1937
01:46:01,231 --> 01:46:02,524
Kill the uplink.

1938
01:46:02,899 --> 01:46:04,734
This thing is gonna blow.

1939
01:46:04,817 --> 01:46:07,779
- We gotta get it off the ship.
- Easy.

1940
01:46:07,862 --> 01:46:09,197
Stand down, Sergeant.

1941
01:46:09,280 --> 01:46:13,201
Shut this bomb down
and let us finish our job the right way.

1942
01:46:13,284 --> 01:46:15,912
I'm under orders to protect
a surface detonation.

1943
01:46:15,995 --> 01:46:18,289
I'm gonna give you three seconds
to shut this bomb down,

1944
01:46:18,373 --> 01:46:20,208
and then I'm gonna make you shoot me.

1945
01:46:21,251 --> 01:46:23,586
Hurry, Watsler. For Christ's sake, hurry.

1946
01:46:26,130 --> 01:46:27,549
[ Detonator Powering Down ]

1947
01:46:27,632 --> 01:46:29,509
What happened?

1948
01:46:30,677 --> 01:46:31,886
Aah!

1949
01:46:32,720 --> 01:46:33,721
[ Grunting ]

1950
01:46:33,805 --> 01:46:37,350
Sir, the override... It's been overridden.

1951
01:46:38,309 --> 01:46:39,394
I bought us a couple of minutes,

1952
01:46:39,477 --> 01:46:41,521
so get that radio workin', okay?
Hurry, hurry!

1953
01:46:42,272 --> 01:46:43,773
[ Grunting ]

1954
01:46:44,148 --> 01:46:47,902
Bring me all the way up here just to
blow me and my friends up? Is that it?

1955
01:46:47,986 --> 01:46:50,738
- [ Gasping ] Listen...
- Shut up!

1956
01:46:50,822 --> 01:46:54,742
Shut up, Colonel. I'm talking now.

1957
01:46:54,826 --> 01:46:56,828
[ Sharp ] It could start again.
It might've been a warning.

1958
01:46:56,911 --> 01:46:58,162
[ Gasping ]

1959
01:46:58,997 --> 01:46:59,956
Uh-oh.

1960
01:47:00,039 --> 01:47:02,458
That's why you are gonna
dismantle this bomb.

1961
01:47:02,542 --> 01:47:05,128
All right. What'd we miss?

1962
01:47:09,632 --> 01:47:12,510
- Do it again.
- Go.

1963
01:47:15,972 --> 01:47:17,890
Keep tryin'.

1964
01:47:19,183 --> 01:47:23,771
Sir, I need you to cease and desist.
I need your terminal... Now.

1965
01:47:27,150 --> 01:47:29,944
- They're reactivating the bomb.
- Comin' back on-line, sir.

1966
01:47:30,028 --> 01:47:33,323
- [ Detonator Blipping ]
- Oh, geez. Here we go again.

1967
01:47:33,406 --> 01:47:36,451
What're you doin' up here? And why
did you even bother to make the trip?

1968
01:47:36,534 --> 01:47:39,120
To do the right thing,
to see that it's done.

1969
01:47:39,203 --> 01:47:41,414
[ Breathing Heavily ]

1970
01:47:42,498 --> 01:47:44,208
[ Gasping ]

1971
01:47:47,045 --> 01:47:50,089
For God's sakes,
think about what you're doin'.

1972
01:47:50,173 --> 01:47:53,635
Why are you listenin' to someone
that's 100,000 miles away?

1973
01:47:53,718 --> 01:47:57,305
We're here.
Nobody down there can help us.

1974
01:47:57,388 --> 01:48:01,184
So if we don't get this job done,
then everybody's gone.

1975
01:48:01,267 --> 01:48:02,810
One minute.

1976
01:48:03,895 --> 01:48:06,606
I've been drillin' holes
in the earth for 30 years.

1977
01:48:06,689 --> 01:48:11,444
And I have never, never missed
a depth that I have aimed for.

1978
01:48:11,527 --> 01:48:14,989
And by God, I am not gonna miss
this one. I will make 800 feet.

1979
01:48:15,073 --> 01:48:16,866
Forty-two seconds.

1980
01:48:18,242 --> 01:48:21,162
But I can't do it alone, Colonel.
I need your help.

1981
01:48:21,245 --> 01:48:24,749
You swear on your daughter's life,
on my family's,

1982
01:48:24,832 --> 01:48:27,502
that you can hit that mark?

1983
01:48:27,585 --> 01:48:31,881
I will make 800 feet.
I swear to God, I will.

1984
01:48:31,964 --> 01:48:34,425
Then let's turn this bomb off.

1985
01:48:35,718 --> 01:48:37,261
[ Beeping ]

1986
01:48:43,851 --> 01:48:45,937
[ Beeping Continues ]

1987
01:48:46,354 --> 01:48:47,939
Steady. Take it back.

1988
01:48:48,022 --> 01:48:49,941
That's what you'll have to do.
Get 'em off backwards.

1989
01:48:50,024 --> 01:48:51,526
Rainbow track? Under...

1990
01:48:51,609 --> 01:48:53,152
- Under one? Under... Okay.
- All of 'em. All of 'em.

1991
01:48:53,236 --> 01:48:56,698
- Okay. Are we free of static?
- Oh, do a good job. Do a good job.

1992
01:48:56,781 --> 01:48:59,075
- Steady. Steady.
- Good job. All right. All right.

1993
01:48:59,158 --> 01:49:02,870
Go! Go! Go! Red wire "A."
Ready? And...

1994
01:49:02,954 --> 01:49:04,747
Now. Come on! Come on!
Come on! Come on!

1995
01:49:04,831 --> 01:49:06,082
[ Breathing Heavily ]

1996
01:49:06,165 --> 01:49:07,250
Negative "B."

1997
01:49:07,333 --> 01:49:10,211
- Ready, and now.
- Do a good job. Do a good job.

1998
01:49:10,294 --> 01:49:11,713
Track flipped. Hot's in.

1999
01:49:11,796 --> 01:49:13,131
- It better be. Go.
- Red or blue?

2000
01:49:13,214 --> 01:49:14,799
[ Beeping Faster ]

2001
01:49:16,300 --> 01:49:17,552
Re...

2002
01:49:20,096 --> 01:49:21,097
[ Whimpering ]

2003
01:49:21,180 --> 01:49:22,682
[ Beeping Continues ]

2004
01:49:22,765 --> 01:49:24,142
Blue.

2005
01:49:24,684 --> 01:49:26,436
[ Beeping Stops ]

2006
01:49:27,186 --> 01:49:28,396
Good job!

2007
01:49:28,479 --> 01:49:30,565
[ All Panting ]

2008
01:49:33,735 --> 01:49:36,195
Oh, God, it sucks up here.

2009
01:49:36,988 --> 01:49:39,699
Sir, the clock has stopped
at three seconds.

2010
01:49:39,782 --> 01:49:41,033
What?

2011
01:49:41,701 --> 01:49:43,870
Have we lost complete radio contact?

2012
01:49:43,953 --> 01:49:45,079
I got some magic happening.

2013
01:49:45,163 --> 01:49:46,497
We're bouncing off Russian
and French satellites.

2014
01:49:46,581 --> 01:49:50,626
- It may have a faint signal.
<i>- Houston? Houston, do you copy?</i>

2015
01:49:52,336 --> 01:49:54,338
<i>Go ahead,</i> Freedom.

2016
01:49:54,672 --> 01:49:55,965
Houston, you have a problem...

2017
01:49:56,048 --> 01:49:57,425
<i>Problem.</i>

2018
01:49:57,508 --> 01:50:00,344
See, I promised my little girl
that I'd be comin' home.

2019
01:50:01,345 --> 01:50:04,223
Now, I don't know what you people
are doin' down there,

2020
01:50:04,307 --> 01:50:05,808
but we got a hole to dig up there.

2021
01:50:05,892 --> 01:50:07,643
[ Cheering ]

2022
01:50:07,727 --> 01:50:09,604
Go, go, go, go! Come on.
We got work to do.

2023
01:50:10,021 --> 01:50:13,441
Okay, guys. All go, no quit.
How ya doin' down there? Good?

2024
01:50:13,524 --> 01:50:16,444
Okay, got the tranny.
We're back in business.

2025
01:50:16,527 --> 01:50:20,364
Hey, you guys should take a break
and come up and see this.

2026
01:50:21,657 --> 01:50:24,452
Wow. Got a great view
of the Earth from here.

2027
01:50:24,535 --> 01:50:26,537
Too bad we'll never
set foot on her again.

2028
01:50:26,621 --> 01:50:29,081
- Lev, do you see anything?
- No.

2029
01:50:29,165 --> 01:50:32,460
Well, keep goin'. I'm not givin' up.

2030
01:50:32,543 --> 01:50:34,462
Hold up here, Bear.

2031
01:50:34,545 --> 01:50:36,631
- [ Lev ] Oh, boy.
- [ A.J. I This is great.

2032
01:50:36,714 --> 01:50:39,634
We just happen to run into
the Grand Canyon on the asteroid?

2033
01:50:39,717 --> 01:50:42,929
I told you, you took a wrong way,
a wrong road.

2034
01:50:43,012 --> 01:50:46,349
[ A.J. I What... What road?
Do you see any roads around here?

2035
01:50:46,432 --> 01:50:50,520
[ Lev ] You know what? I do not have
much pleasure being near God's ear.

2036
01:50:50,603 --> 01:50:53,147
But you think this is
looking good, or what?

2037
01:50:53,231 --> 01:50:57,443
Lev, why don't you just do humanity
a favour and just shut the hell up?

2038
01:51:02,782 --> 01:51:04,617
Have you ever heard of Evel Knievel?

2039
01:51:04,700 --> 01:51:07,078
No, I never saw <i>Star Wars.</i>

2040
01:51:13,084 --> 01:51:15,545
All right. Doin' a good job.

2041
01:51:15,628 --> 01:51:18,339
- Give me a depth reading, Max.
- We're 150 feet, Harry.

2042
01:51:18,422 --> 01:51:22,009
[ Humming <i>William Tell Overture ]</i>

2043
01:51:22,510 --> 01:51:23,678
Yee-ha!

2044
01:51:23,761 --> 01:51:27,306
Ride 'em, cowboy!
Yippee-kai-yo, kai-yay!

2045
01:51:27,390 --> 01:51:31,811
Get off the nuclear warhead.

2046
01:51:31,894 --> 01:51:34,564
I was doin' that guy from that movie,
you know, Slim Pickens,

2047
01:51:34,647 --> 01:51:37,108
where he rides it all the way in,
the nuclear warhead.

2048
01:51:37,191 --> 01:51:40,069
- Now.
- Oh, you didn't see that one, huh?

2049
01:51:40,152 --> 01:51:43,030
We got 700 feet of hole to dig,
Rockhound.

2050
01:51:43,114 --> 01:51:47,702
All right. Just... Just wanted to feel
the power between my legs, brother.

2051
01:51:48,828 --> 01:51:50,788
Hey, Sharp.

2052
01:51:50,872 --> 01:51:53,749
[ Chanting ] No nukes!
No nukes! No nukes!

2053
01:51:53,833 --> 01:51:55,835
You got any more bullets
in that gun, Sharp?

2054
01:51:56,168 --> 01:51:58,337
[ A.J. I What did Watts tell you, Bear?
If she kicked you in the balls,

2055
01:51:58,421 --> 01:51:59,547
- you'd keep floating.
- Yeah.

2056
01:51:59,630 --> 01:52:01,299
[ Engine Roaring ]

2057
01:52:02,466 --> 01:52:04,844
[ A.J. I We turn the thrusters off,
we jump this thing,

2058
01:52:04,927 --> 01:52:06,637
we float right over it.

2059
01:52:07,221 --> 01:52:09,223
Go over it again, Lev.

2060
01:52:09,307 --> 01:52:12,685
Throw the jet thrusters off
exactly when we jump.

2061
01:52:12,768 --> 01:52:14,270
- Okay.
- And then we're gonna put them on,

2062
01:52:14,353 --> 01:52:16,397
and we gonna go down nice and slow.

2063
01:52:16,480 --> 01:52:20,067
- That's it. That's it, baby. That's it.
- Is this gonna work?

2064
01:52:20,151 --> 01:52:24,238
- I don't know.
- Lev, you know what, just lie to me.

2065
01:52:24,322 --> 01:52:28,242
Let's say 50-50... No. More like, uh...

2066
01:52:28,326 --> 01:52:31,370
Like 70-30 or 80-20.
But you know what?

2067
01:52:31,454 --> 01:52:35,917
If it works, the two of you
gonna be heroes, just like me.

2068
01:52:36,000 --> 01:52:38,836
Screw it.
We're jumpin' over this canyon.

2069
01:52:43,007 --> 01:52:46,010
Just for the record,
this is a very bad idea!

2070
01:52:49,472 --> 01:52:50,556
Wait for the edge.

2071
01:52:50,640 --> 01:52:52,808
- Don't hit it till we get there.
- I'm waiting.

2072
01:52:53,684 --> 01:52:55,978
- [ Lev ] Three.
- [ A.J. Chattering ]

2073
01:52:57,021 --> 01:52:59,440
[ Lev ] Two. One!

2074
01:52:59,523 --> 01:53:00,942
Aah!

2075
01:53:09,325 --> 01:53:12,620
- Yes! It's working!
- It's working!

2076
01:53:12,703 --> 01:53:13,871
[ Lev ] Oh, my God!

2077
01:53:13,955 --> 01:53:15,206
[ All Shouting ]

2078
01:53:15,289 --> 01:53:20,586
- I'm a genius! Wait a minute.
- Whoa. Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

2079
01:53:20,670 --> 01:53:22,755
- We got some rocks!
- Go left! Go left!

2080
01:53:22,838 --> 01:53:25,424
Lev, Lev, I can't do anything!

2081
01:53:25,508 --> 01:53:26,634
[ All Screaming ]

2082
01:53:26,717 --> 01:53:28,344
[ Crashing ]

2083
01:53:35,184 --> 01:53:37,812
Oh, okay, okay,
we're floating into outer space.

2084
01:53:37,895 --> 01:53:39,313
- Check main switch.
- Uh, this could be

2085
01:53:39,397 --> 01:53:41,440
a little bit of a problem.

2086
01:53:41,524 --> 01:53:43,693
- Thrusters on... Now!
- All right, turn 'em on.

2087
01:53:43,776 --> 01:53:45,277
[ Rattling ]

2088
01:53:46,862 --> 01:53:48,531
- What's wrong?
- I... I don't know.

2089
01:53:48,614 --> 01:53:52,118
The... The thrusters not working.
I hate this machine!

2090
01:53:52,201 --> 01:53:53,327
I thought you had this planned!

2091
01:53:53,411 --> 01:53:55,079
- What're we supposed to do?
- Be quiet! I must think!

2092
01:53:55,162 --> 01:53:57,832
- I'm stepping outside.
- You're... You're going outside?

2093
01:53:57,915 --> 01:54:03,421
I am the only certified astronaut,
and I'm saving your American ass!

2094
01:54:05,006 --> 01:54:06,382
[ Grunts ]

2095
01:54:07,633 --> 01:54:10,094
Yes. You'll listen to him. Right.

2096
01:54:15,266 --> 01:54:19,061
Hurry up, Lev, because we're
about a mile off the asteroid!

2097
01:54:19,145 --> 01:54:22,481
Just a second. The fuel line is iced up.

2098
01:54:22,565 --> 01:54:26,610
- I think maybe workin' now.
- No, Lev, it's not working!

2099
01:54:26,694 --> 01:54:29,613
I'm sorry, A.J., I was way off the odds.

2100
01:54:29,697 --> 01:54:31,115
[ Bear ] We're gettin' higher, man.

2101
01:54:31,198 --> 01:54:34,577
Look out! The rocks! Rocks are coming!

2102
01:54:36,245 --> 01:54:39,707
[ Moaning, Grunting ]

2103
01:54:40,833 --> 01:54:42,376
Hold on!

2104
01:54:42,460 --> 01:54:45,129
Aah!

2105
01:54:46,797 --> 01:54:49,550
- Pull the thrusters!
- Lev, look out!

2106
01:54:51,510 --> 01:54:53,429
[ All Screaming ]

2107
01:54:56,557 --> 01:54:58,392
- We lost Lev.
- A.J.!

2108
01:54:58,476 --> 01:54:59,685
[ Grunting ]

2109
01:54:59,769 --> 01:55:02,063
A.J., the thrusters!

2110
01:55:02,146 --> 01:55:03,272
Aah!

2111
01:55:06,275 --> 01:55:08,027
Let's get Lev back!

2112
01:55:08,486 --> 01:55:10,404
Aah!

2113
01:55:11,655 --> 01:55:13,074
[ Gasping ]

2114
01:55:16,494 --> 01:55:19,246
Lev, hold on! We're comin' in!

2115
01:55:20,372 --> 01:55:22,583
[ Grunting ]

2116
01:55:26,837 --> 01:55:28,506
[ Grunting ]

2117
01:55:30,549 --> 01:55:33,177
[ All Panting ]

2118
01:55:35,846 --> 01:55:37,723
Thank You, Jesus. Thank You, Lord.

2119
01:55:37,807 --> 01:55:39,517
Thank You. Thank You,
thank You, thank You, thank You.

2120
01:55:40,142 --> 01:55:42,978
[ Grunting ] Lev!

2121
01:55:43,687 --> 01:55:48,317
- Now I'm really a Russian hero!
- I told you!

2122
01:55:48,400 --> 01:55:50,778
- I know!
- I knew this would work!

2123
01:55:50,861 --> 01:55:53,197
- Good odds, you know?
- Come on, Lev.

2124
01:55:53,280 --> 01:55:55,950
- Get in here. We gotta go.
- Yah!

2125
01:55:56,283 --> 01:55:58,369
[ Rumbling ]

2126
01:55:59,578 --> 01:56:01,831
Rockhound, keep on that transmission.

2127
01:56:01,914 --> 01:56:04,959
- Tranny looks good, Harry.
- All right. Take it outta there.

2128
01:56:05,042 --> 01:56:07,002
Lock it down, Chick.

2129
01:56:08,712 --> 01:56:10,256
Nice.

2130
01:56:11,340 --> 01:56:14,552
How come we didn't get
any training on this thing?

2131
01:56:14,635 --> 01:56:18,264
Whoa. Very cool. I could take out
this asteroid single-handedly.

2132
01:56:18,347 --> 01:56:19,348
[ Machine Whirring ]

2133
01:56:19,431 --> 01:56:21,475
Okay, boys, give it a rest.
I'll take it from here.

2134
01:56:21,559 --> 01:56:22,685
[ Machine Gun Firing ]

2135
01:56:22,768 --> 01:56:24,353
Whoa!

2136
01:56:24,645 --> 01:56:26,355
- What the hell is that?
- It's Rockhound.

2137
01:56:26,438 --> 01:56:29,692
Whoa. This is so much fun, it's freaky.

2138
01:56:31,235 --> 01:56:32,194
Rockhound!

2139
01:56:32,278 --> 01:56:33,320
[ Cheering ]

2140
01:56:33,571 --> 01:56:35,739
Whoa, watch your heads. Sorry, Harry.

2141
01:56:38,450 --> 01:56:40,828
- Outta my way, boys!
- Rockhound!

2142
01:56:40,911 --> 01:56:43,539
Meet your maker, asteroid!

2143
01:56:43,622 --> 01:56:44,915
[ Both Grunting ]

2144
01:56:48,252 --> 01:56:50,004
What the hell's the matter with you,
Rockhound?

2145
01:56:50,087 --> 01:56:52,006
- Goddamn!
- This is insane.

2146
01:56:52,089 --> 01:56:53,632
- Have you lost your mind?
- No.

2147
01:56:53,716 --> 01:56:57,928
He's got space dementia.
Harry, you want to watch your man.

2148
01:57:00,389 --> 01:57:05,144
Max, downshift and put it in reverse.
We gotta get that pipe outta there.

2149
01:57:05,227 --> 01:57:06,395
[ Max ] Uh-oh.

2150
01:57:06,478 --> 01:57:07,521
[ Grunts ]

2151
01:57:07,605 --> 01:57:09,773
[ Loud Rumbling ]

2152
01:57:09,857 --> 01:57:12,193
- What's happening?
- The ground's cracking!

2153
01:57:12,276 --> 01:57:13,444
Earthquake!

2154
01:57:21,660 --> 01:57:23,537
Quick, shut it off!

2155
01:57:24,955 --> 01:57:28,334
- Shut it off! Shut it off now!
- We're gonna have a blowout!

2156
01:57:28,417 --> 01:57:31,045
- We hit a gas pocket!
- We got pressure out the ass!

2157
01:57:31,128 --> 01:57:33,214
[ Grunting ]

2158
01:57:33,297 --> 01:57:36,675
Max, get your helmet on!
Max, she's gonna blow!

2159
01:57:36,759 --> 01:57:40,054
- Aah! Oh, Jesus, I'm cooking!
- Max, get outta there!

2160
01:57:40,137 --> 01:57:44,475
This is it! Harry!

2161
01:57:46,977 --> 01:57:49,021
I'm bailing!

2162
01:57:52,107 --> 01:57:53,651
Max!

2163
01:57:56,320 --> 01:57:57,321
Goodbye, Max.

2164
01:57:57,404 --> 01:58:00,866
- Max!
- Take care, buddy.

2165
01:58:00,950 --> 01:58:03,035
- Armadillo's off the scope.
- I think we've had a blowout.

2166
01:58:03,118 --> 01:58:04,703
No sign of the Armadillo.

2167
01:58:04,787 --> 01:58:06,956
[ All Shouting ]

2168
01:58:36,277 --> 01:58:38,153
Get a hold of Truman.

2169
01:58:39,780 --> 01:58:41,615
Prepare the world for bad news.

2170
01:58:42,366 --> 01:58:45,744
[ Air Raid Sirens Wailing ]

2171
01:58:49,290 --> 01:58:51,667
<i>[ Male Newscaster#1 ] We're getting
sketchy information that the mission</i>

2172
01:58:51,750 --> 01:58:54,128
<i>has suffered massive failure.</i>

2173
01:58:54,211 --> 01:58:56,797
<i>And what we're trying to do right now
is to confirm that</i>

2174
01:58:56,880 --> 01:58:58,382
<i>and find out exactly what that means.</i>

2175
01:58:58,465 --> 01:59:01,635
<i>Repeat. We're getting leaks
from several NASA officials,</i>

2176
01:59:01,719 --> 01:59:03,470
<i>some rushing home
to be with their families,</i>

2177
01:59:03,554 --> 01:59:07,266
<i>that the drilling was unsuccessful.</i>

2178
01:59:08,392 --> 01:59:11,395
[ Chanting ]

2179
01:59:11,770 --> 01:59:15,941
<i>[Female Newscaster
Speaking French ]</i>

2180
01:59:16,066 --> 01:59:18,944
<i>[ Male Newscaster#2]
This could very well be our final hour.</i>

2181
01:59:19,028 --> 01:59:22,364
<i>[ Male Newscaster#3
Speaking Foreign Language ]</i>

2182
01:59:22,448 --> 01:59:24,450
<i>[ Male Newscaster#4 ]
We're gonna go off the air now.</i>

2183
01:59:24,533 --> 01:59:26,827
<i>Good luck and God bless.</i>

2184
01:59:31,081 --> 01:59:32,916
<i>- [ Man #1 ] We've got incoming.
- [ Man #2] I got tracks.</i>

2185
01:59:33,000 --> 01:59:35,627
NORAD's tracking four small
incoming over Europe.

2186
01:59:35,711 --> 01:59:37,046
I think one's about to hit near Paris.

2187
01:59:40,174 --> 01:59:42,468
[ Asteroid Shrieking ]

2188
01:59:44,636 --> 01:59:46,597
[ Screaming ]

2189
02:00:01,195 --> 02:00:02,696
[ All Shouting ]

2190
02:00:03,447 --> 02:00:04,907
<i>Reports are coming in.</i>

2191
02:00:04,990 --> 02:00:07,534
<i>[ Male Newscaster#1 ] Martial law
has been implemented in 42 countries.</i>

2192
02:00:07,618 --> 02:00:10,079
<i>[ Male Newscaster#2]
Once the asteroid hits zero barrier,</i>

2193
02:00:10,162 --> 02:00:14,416
<i>it will take about three hours
and 57 minutes to impact Earth.</i>

2194
02:00:14,583 --> 02:00:16,460
<i>[ Sirens Wailing]</i>

2195
02:00:18,504 --> 02:00:21,131
I guess we do it the president's way.
I'll order an evac.

2196
02:00:21,215 --> 02:00:22,466
You can remote detonate.

2197
02:00:22,549 --> 02:00:24,176
You still don't think this'll work, do you?

2198
02:00:24,259 --> 02:00:25,928
What I think is irrelevant.

2199
02:00:26,011 --> 02:00:29,098
- [ Kimsey ] We need to do it now.
- Fine.

2200
02:00:29,181 --> 02:00:31,350
- Can they still take off?
- We hope so.

2201
02:00:31,433 --> 02:00:33,477
You are the one that
pulled them into this!

2202
02:00:33,560 --> 02:00:37,064
That is my family up there,
so I don't wanna hear, "We hope so"!

2203
02:00:42,653 --> 02:00:46,365
Guess what, guys?
It's time to embrace the horror.

2204
02:00:46,448 --> 02:00:49,952
Look. We got front-row tickets
to the end of the Earth.

2205
02:00:50,994 --> 02:00:52,830
<i>[ Radio Static Crackling]</i>

2206
02:01:01,588 --> 02:01:03,715
[ Rumbling ]

2207
02:01:12,057 --> 02:01:13,517
Yeah!

2208
02:01:13,600 --> 02:01:14,893
Way to go, baby!

2209
02:01:14,977 --> 02:01:16,311
Harry!

2210
02:01:19,148 --> 02:01:22,359
[ All Cheering ]

2211
02:01:23,277 --> 02:01:25,571
<i>Yo, Harry! What's up, baby?</i>

2212
02:01:25,654 --> 02:01:28,323
<i>Hey, get that bomb outta there!
We got a hole to make!</i>

2213
02:01:29,741 --> 02:01:31,618
<i>[ Sharp]
Houston, you're not gonna believe this,</i>

2214
02:01:31,702 --> 02:01:33,036
<i>but the other Armadillo has arrived.</i>

2215
02:01:33,120 --> 02:01:35,164
[ Cheering, Applauding ]

2216
02:01:35,247 --> 02:01:38,208
All right, people, listen up.
Settle down and focus.

2217
02:01:38,292 --> 02:01:40,711
- Mechanical, get on-line.
- P.P.O., gimme a setup.

2218
02:01:40,794 --> 02:01:42,713
Your boyfriend's back.

2219
02:01:43,213 --> 02:01:44,256
[ Bear ] Yo, Harry!

2220
02:01:44,339 --> 02:01:46,091
[ Shouting ]

2221
02:01:47,217 --> 02:01:49,219
Hey, Harry. You miss me?

2222
02:01:49,303 --> 02:01:52,723
A.J., I got just five words for ya.

2223
02:01:52,806 --> 02:01:55,976
- Damn glad to see ya, boy!
- That's six words.

2224
02:01:56,059 --> 02:01:57,352
Chick, walk 'em down.

2225
02:01:57,436 --> 02:01:58,979
[ A.J. I So where's this hole
you need dug?

2226
02:01:59,605 --> 02:02:02,232
<i>[ Watts]
Houston, drilling has recommenced.</i>

2227
02:02:02,316 --> 02:02:05,903
Do you think they can drill
250 feet in an hour?

2228
02:02:05,986 --> 02:02:07,488
They better.

2229
02:02:07,821 --> 02:02:09,531
Bring that piece on in, Bear.

2230
02:02:10,532 --> 02:02:12,201
Tractor pull.

2231
02:02:12,910 --> 02:02:16,663
- I'm comin' down!
- We got 250 feet to go.

2232
02:02:16,747 --> 02:02:19,750
It's our last transmission, last drill head.

2233
02:02:19,833 --> 02:02:23,337
Punch it through.
First gear. We got contact.

2234
02:02:24,046 --> 02:02:25,422
Come on down, A.J.

2235
02:02:25,506 --> 02:02:26,965
[ Grunting ]

2236
02:02:27,674 --> 02:02:28,926
I got this, man. Let's go!

2237
02:02:29,009 --> 02:02:30,677
Lev, the right engine hub.

2238
02:02:30,761 --> 02:02:33,013
Houston, I'm getting no response
from the preflight sequence.

2239
02:02:33,096 --> 02:02:36,683
[ Muffled ] Come on, now.
This is not... Hey... Hey, come here.

2240
02:02:36,767 --> 02:02:39,061
Can you get me outta here, please, Lev?
Thank you.

2241
02:02:39,144 --> 02:02:40,479
[ Grunting ]

2242
02:02:40,938 --> 02:02:43,982
- Ow! Jesus! Hey!
- Wait. Uh, shh, shh.

2243
02:02:44,066 --> 02:02:45,192
<i>- [ Watts] Lev, the right engine...</i>
- Okay.

2244
02:02:45,275 --> 02:02:49,780
Lemme outta here, will ya?
Just tryin' to have some fun before I die!

2245
02:02:49,863 --> 02:02:53,492
- How deep are we?
- Seven seventy.

2246
02:02:55,953 --> 02:02:57,746
[ Grunting ]

2247
02:02:58,789 --> 02:03:00,916
- Whoa, they got problems.
- The gauges are spiking.

2248
02:03:00,999 --> 02:03:03,001
Methane! Shut it down! Back it down!

2249
02:03:03,085 --> 02:03:05,128
I can't pull back now.
The bit'll get lodged.

2250
02:03:05,212 --> 02:03:07,214
We don't have enough time!

2251
02:03:07,297 --> 02:03:10,968
Whoa, whoa, whoa! It's gonna blow!
It's how we lost Max!

2252
02:03:11,051 --> 02:03:13,262
I know what I'm talkin' about.
We can punch through this.

2253
02:03:13,345 --> 02:03:14,930
We can knock this outta the park.

2254
02:03:15,013 --> 02:03:16,848
This is our last transmission, A.J.

2255
02:03:16,932 --> 02:03:19,142
Goddamn it, if you're ever
gonna trust me, ever,

2256
02:03:19,226 --> 02:03:22,104
once in your life, trust me now!

2257
02:03:22,187 --> 02:03:23,897
Harry, it's gonna blow!

2258
02:03:23,981 --> 02:03:27,067
Harry, I know what I'm doin'.
You just gotta trust me.

2259
02:03:28,527 --> 02:03:30,487
Make the call.

2260
02:03:32,739 --> 02:03:35,158
All right. Hold on.
I'm pushin' through her.

2261
02:03:39,746 --> 02:03:40,789
[ Grunting ]

2262
02:03:40,872 --> 02:03:42,874
I'm pushin' through her!

2263
02:03:43,584 --> 02:03:46,753
- What's your depth?
- Seven seventy-five. Seven eighty.

2264
02:03:46,837 --> 02:03:49,131
Take it up, baby! Ram it home!

2265
02:03:49,715 --> 02:03:51,592
[ Grunts ] Drive on down, A.J.!

2266
02:03:51,675 --> 02:03:54,261
Seven eighty-five. Come on. Come on.

2267
02:03:54,344 --> 02:03:56,513
- Come on, A.J.!
- Punch it!

2268
02:03:56,597 --> 02:03:57,598
Ninety-one. Come on.

2269
02:03:57,681 --> 02:04:00,767
Seven ninety-two. Seven ninety-five!

2270
02:04:00,851 --> 02:04:03,020
Drive it down, A.J.!

2271
02:04:03,103 --> 02:04:06,023
Seven ninety-seven! Ninety-nine!

2272
02:04:06,106 --> 02:04:09,776
- Breakthrough!
- Eight hundred! Eight-oh-two, Harry!

2273
02:04:09,860 --> 02:04:11,570
- Yeah!
- We did it!

2274
02:04:11,653 --> 02:04:13,280
[ All Cheering ]

2275
02:04:13,488 --> 02:04:15,032
- Yes!
- We did it!

2276
02:04:15,115 --> 02:04:19,244
- Yeah! Kid, way to go!
- I knew it, baby!

2277
02:04:19,328 --> 02:04:21,330
It's not over till we get
the bomb down that hole.

2278
02:04:21,413 --> 02:04:23,081
Watts, they've got 38 minutes.

2279
02:04:44,019 --> 02:04:45,562
[ Sharp ] Harry,
you've gotta give me that hole.

2280
02:04:45,646 --> 02:04:48,690
I'm gonna need two more minutes.
I got a bent pipe jammed in the hole.

2281
02:04:48,774 --> 02:04:52,486
We gotta cut it out before
we can send that bomb down. A.J.!

2282
02:04:52,569 --> 02:04:54,613
- She good to go?
- Yeah, I'm all set.

2283
02:04:54,696 --> 02:04:56,073
All right.

2284
02:04:56,823 --> 02:04:58,116
[ Grunts ]

2285
02:05:01,453 --> 02:05:03,622
- All right.
<i>- [ Harry]A.J., come on! Make it fast!</i>

2286
02:05:03,705 --> 02:05:07,000
I'm goin' as fast as I can!
There's a lot of gas pressure!

2287
02:05:13,924 --> 02:05:15,008
You feel that?

2288
02:05:15,092 --> 02:05:17,260
Harry, you gotta give me that hole.
The bomb is almost ready.

2289
02:05:17,344 --> 02:05:19,930
<i>- [ Harry] Pull that pipe out!</i>
- Harry, I'm almost through!

2290
02:05:20,013 --> 02:05:21,014
Give me 15 more seconds!

2291
02:05:21,598 --> 02:05:23,100
[ Rumbling ]

2292
02:05:27,187 --> 02:05:29,314
Well, this is somethin' new.

2293
02:05:30,899 --> 02:05:31,900
[ Crashing ]

2294
02:05:31,983 --> 02:05:33,026
I don't think this thing likes us.

2295
02:05:33,110 --> 02:05:36,154
That's 'cause it knows
we're here to kill it.

2296
02:05:36,238 --> 02:05:37,364
Whoa!

2297
02:05:41,368 --> 02:05:43,370
Hey, what's goin' on up there?

2298
02:05:48,125 --> 02:05:49,543
A.J.!

2299
02:05:50,919 --> 02:05:53,213
- What the hell was that?
- A.J.!

2300
02:05:53,797 --> 02:05:55,841
Goddamn it, I'm finished!

2301
02:05:56,633 --> 02:05:59,469
- A.J., you all right?
- Oh, lot of gas pressure in here, man!

2302
02:05:59,553 --> 02:06:02,222
- Get me out!
- Whoa, whoa, whoa! Hydrogen pocket!

2303
02:06:02,305 --> 02:06:03,515
Aah!

2304
02:06:12,023 --> 02:06:13,316
<i>Whoa!</i>

2305
02:06:16,737 --> 02:06:18,989
- [ Grunts ]
- Aah!

2306
02:06:19,489 --> 02:06:22,659
Oh! Harry! Pull me in!

2307
02:06:24,494 --> 02:06:25,662
[ Grunting ]

2308
02:06:25,746 --> 02:06:28,206
Aah! A.J., hang on!

2309
02:06:28,790 --> 02:06:30,500
[ Grunting ]

2310
02:06:34,296 --> 02:06:36,006
Secure the bomb!

2311
02:06:37,174 --> 02:06:39,009
Sharp, heads up!

2312
02:06:39,801 --> 02:06:42,304
Gruber! Get outta there now!

2313
02:06:42,846 --> 02:06:43,805
[ Asteroids Shrieking ]

2314
02:06:43,889 --> 02:06:45,307
Oh, no.

2315
02:06:51,938 --> 02:06:52,981
[ Whimpering ]

2316
02:06:53,190 --> 02:06:55,150
Oh, God, no!

2317
02:06:55,776 --> 02:06:57,694
[ All Screaming ]

2318
02:07:01,698 --> 02:07:03,283
Look out!

2319
02:07:06,244 --> 02:07:09,372
Help! Oh, no!

2320
02:07:10,665 --> 02:07:12,626
[ Screaming ]

2321
02:07:15,378 --> 02:07:16,588
[ Panting ]

2322
02:07:16,671 --> 02:07:18,089
Do you believe that just happened?

2323
02:07:18,173 --> 02:07:19,633
[ Gas Hissing ]

2324
02:07:22,302 --> 02:07:24,429
- Sharp, you all right?
- I'm okay.

2325
02:07:24,513 --> 02:07:26,973
- Bear?
- Yeah. I'm here, Harry.

2326
02:07:27,057 --> 02:07:29,559
- A.J.?
- Yeah, I'm okay.

2327
02:07:29,643 --> 02:07:30,977
[ Gas Hissing ]

2328
02:07:32,187 --> 02:07:33,730
We lost Gruber.

2329
02:07:35,398 --> 02:07:36,900
Gruber's dead.

2330
02:07:37,651 --> 02:07:39,402
Let's get that bomb ready and go home.

2331
02:07:47,410 --> 02:07:48,495
[ Sharp ] Oh, my God.

2332
02:07:48,578 --> 02:07:50,205
[ Beeping ]

2333
02:07:50,288 --> 02:07:52,165
Is there a problem, Colonel?

2334
02:07:52,249 --> 02:07:54,835
The timer, the remote,
the whole thing's dead.

2335
02:07:54,918 --> 02:07:57,003
What, the bomb is dead?

2336
02:07:57,087 --> 02:07:58,421
No, the trigger's dead.

2337
02:07:58,505 --> 02:08:01,675
It must've gotten damaged
during the rock storm.

2338
02:08:03,093 --> 02:08:05,095
So how do we detonate it?

2339
02:08:14,896 --> 02:08:19,192
We have 18 minutes to zero barrier.
We got some bad news.

2340
02:08:19,901 --> 02:08:23,697
The remote detonator on the bomb
has been damaged.

2341
02:08:23,780 --> 02:08:26,658
That means that somebody's
gonna have to stay behind.

2342
02:08:28,743 --> 02:08:31,246
It takes two people to fly this thing.

2343
02:08:31,329 --> 02:08:35,125
Either we all stay and die,
or you guys draw straws.

2344
02:08:36,001 --> 02:08:39,838
I say we all stay and die. But that's me.

2345
02:08:40,881 --> 02:08:44,342
I'll draw. Let's draw.

2346
02:08:45,093 --> 02:08:48,013
Nobody's gonna draw straws.

2347
02:08:48,096 --> 02:08:49,389
I'll stay and take care of it.

2348
02:08:49,472 --> 02:08:51,516
- Well, I can't live with that sort of thing.
- Nobody asked you

2349
02:08:51,600 --> 02:08:52,809
- if you could live with it, all right?
- Bullshit!

2350
02:08:52,893 --> 02:08:55,478
No way I will let you volunteer for this

2351
02:08:55,562 --> 02:08:59,441
so I can go back to my home country
like the man who didn't volunteer.

2352
02:08:59,524 --> 02:09:01,151
No way!

2353
02:09:01,234 --> 02:09:05,697
Hey, man, let's draw, and let's see
who's gonna stay up here and dance.

2354
02:09:05,780 --> 02:09:08,533
Guys, I... I know you guys
think I'm crazy right now,

2355
02:09:08,617 --> 02:09:11,620
but I would really like this responsibility.

2356
02:09:12,412 --> 02:09:15,582
- All right. All right.
- I can do it.

2357
02:09:15,665 --> 02:09:17,500
Let's just draw straws
and get it over with. Come on.

2358
02:09:17,584 --> 02:09:19,252
I ain't drawin' against you, Harry.

2359
02:09:19,336 --> 02:09:20,795
Well, I'm gonna draw
against you, Chick,

2360
02:09:20,879 --> 02:09:23,548
so you better just go ahead and do it.

2361
02:09:24,257 --> 02:09:26,092
Just gimme this thing.

2362
02:09:33,767 --> 02:09:35,977
Is this good or bad?

2363
02:09:41,733 --> 02:09:43,276
Oh, man.

2364
02:09:44,569 --> 02:09:47,447
Well, we all gotta die, right?

2365
02:09:50,700 --> 02:09:53,662
I'm the guy who gets
to do it saving the world.

2366
02:09:53,745 --> 02:09:57,332
So, uh, let's go.
We... We got about ten minutes, right?

2367
02:09:59,209 --> 02:10:01,336
You plug this into the port.

2368
02:10:01,419 --> 02:10:05,590
Lift, press, hold. That's it.

2369
02:10:05,674 --> 02:10:10,220
Lift, press, hold. Shouldn't be too tough.
Even I can't screw this up.

2370
02:10:10,303 --> 02:10:12,097
I'll take him down.

2371
02:10:47,507 --> 02:10:52,554
Do me a favour, will ya?
Just tell Grace that, uh...

2372
02:10:52,637 --> 02:10:55,390
That I'll always be with her, okay?

2373
02:10:57,434 --> 02:10:59,394
Can you do that?

2374
02:11:00,937 --> 02:11:03,273
Yeah. Okay, kid.

2375
02:11:09,946 --> 02:11:11,698
Give this to Truman.

2376
02:11:11,781 --> 02:11:14,951
Make sure Truman gets that.
Get in there.

2377
02:11:20,915 --> 02:11:22,584
It's my turn now.

2378
02:11:22,667 --> 02:11:26,337
[ Gasping ] Harry! Harry!

2379
02:11:26,421 --> 02:11:30,967
You can't do this to me! It's my job!

2380
02:11:31,968 --> 02:11:35,972
You go take care of my little girl now.
That's your job.

2381
02:11:39,517 --> 02:11:43,146
Always thought of you as a son. Always.

2382
02:11:43,897 --> 02:11:47,025
But I'd be damn proud
to have you marry Grace.

2383
02:11:48,151 --> 02:11:51,488
- Harry.
- You take care of yourself.

2384
02:11:51,571 --> 02:11:52,864
- Harry, no!
- I love you, pal.

2385
02:11:52,947 --> 02:11:56,242
Harry, I love you! Don't, Harry!
Wait a minute!

2386
02:11:56,326 --> 02:11:58,661
- My son.
- Don't do this, Harry!

2387
02:11:58,745 --> 02:12:01,623
Don't do this! Harry!

2388
02:12:09,923 --> 02:12:12,008
What happened?

2389
02:12:12,092 --> 02:12:14,552
That crazy, stubborn son of a...

2390
02:12:16,930 --> 02:12:18,348
[ Grunting ]

2391
02:12:21,351 --> 02:12:23,686
Well, this was a real good idea.

2392
02:12:24,646 --> 02:12:28,149
All right, let's go, Sharp.
Let's get our team outta here.

2393
02:12:33,488 --> 02:12:37,992
Come on! Let's get ready
to initiate thrusters! Let's go!

2394
02:12:38,076 --> 02:12:40,829
- Strap it in, guys!
- Get the O2 masks.

2395
02:12:40,912 --> 02:12:43,456
Are they green? Are they green?

2396
02:12:43,540 --> 02:12:45,667
I can't believe this is
going down like this.

2397
02:12:45,750 --> 02:12:47,168
You all right?

2398
02:12:47,252 --> 02:12:50,505
- O2 vents locked, pressure loaded.
- Engine board is green.

2399
02:12:53,258 --> 02:12:56,010
<i>[ Woman ] T minus three minutes
and counting.</i>

2400
02:12:56,094 --> 02:12:58,805
Houston, do you copy?
This is Harry Stamper.

2401
02:12:59,931 --> 02:13:01,558
It's down there.

2402
02:13:03,726 --> 02:13:08,189
<i>- Electrical systems primed.
- A.P.U. is set. Oxidizers are loading.</i>

2403
02:13:08,690 --> 02:13:12,235
<i>[ Man ] Houston, we're outta here
in T minus three minutes.</i>

2404
02:13:13,194 --> 02:13:15,280
Daddy! [ Chuckling ]

2405
02:13:15,363 --> 02:13:18,658
Hi, Gracie. Hi, honey.

2406
02:13:19,159 --> 02:13:22,620
<i>Grace, I know I promised you
I was comin' home.</i>

2407
02:13:23,913 --> 02:13:25,915
I don't under... Understand.

2408
02:13:26,541 --> 02:13:30,086
<i>[ Sighs] Looks like I'm gonna
have to break that promise.</i>

2409
02:13:32,630 --> 02:13:36,551
I, um... I lied to you, too,

2410
02:13:36,634 --> 02:13:39,846
when I told you that
I didn't want to be like you.

2411
02:13:41,514 --> 02:13:43,433
Because I am like you.

2412
02:13:44,225 --> 02:13:48,479
And everything good that I have
inside of me, I have from you.

2413
02:13:49,772 --> 02:13:51,858
<i>I love you so much, Daddy.</i>

2414
02:13:52,442 --> 02:13:54,235
I'm so proud of you.

2415
02:13:55,028 --> 02:13:56,988
<i>I'm so scared.</i>

2416
02:13:57,071 --> 02:13:58,740
<i>I'm so scared.</i>

2417
02:13:59,866 --> 02:14:04,537
I know it, baby, but there won't be
anything to be scared of soon.

2418
02:14:07,123 --> 02:14:11,961
<i>Gracie, I want you to know
that A.J. saved us. He did.</i>

2419
02:14:14,380 --> 02:14:16,299
<i>I want you to tell Chick</i>

2420
02:14:16,382 --> 02:14:19,677
<i>that I couldn't have done it without him,
none of it.</i>

2421
02:14:21,804 --> 02:14:24,140
<i>I want you to take care of A.J.</i>

2422
02:14:28,645 --> 02:14:31,481
I wish I could be there
to walk you down the aisle.

2423
02:14:34,901 --> 02:14:36,319
But I'll...

2424
02:14:38,529 --> 02:14:42,283
[ Sighs ] I'll look in on you
from time to time, okay, honey?

2425
02:14:44,827 --> 02:14:46,287
I love you, Grace.

2426
02:14:46,371 --> 02:14:48,498
[ Crying ] I love you, too.

2427
02:14:48,581 --> 02:14:51,376
- I gotta go now, honey.
- Daddy, no.

2428
02:14:52,168 --> 02:14:54,837
No, no, Dad, no.

2429
02:14:56,673 --> 02:15:00,134
<i>[ Man On Radio, Voice Muffled]</i>

2430
02:15:01,678 --> 02:15:05,223
[ Watts ] O.M.S. pod pre-start.
O2 vents locked, pressure loaded.

2431
02:15:07,183 --> 02:15:09,602
What the hell's goin' on up there?
Why haven't you guys left yet?

2432
02:15:09,686 --> 02:15:12,105
We're going, Harry. Houston.

2433
02:15:12,188 --> 02:15:14,983
- We got O.M.S. pod pre-start.
- Pod pre-start confirmed.

2434
02:15:16,818 --> 02:15:18,152
[ Choking ]

2435
02:15:18,611 --> 02:15:19,654
- What's the problem?
- I don't know.

2436
02:15:19,737 --> 02:15:21,114
- What's wrong?
- Fix it now!

2437
02:15:23,157 --> 02:15:25,285
No time, no time!

2438
02:15:25,368 --> 02:15:27,328
- What?
- What's that?

2439
02:15:31,207 --> 02:15:33,459
- Where you goin'?
- Come on. We're stayin', we're goin'.

2440
02:15:33,543 --> 02:15:35,461
We're stayin', we're goin'.
Make up your minds.

2441
02:15:35,545 --> 02:15:38,715
Sharp, get out of here now.
You got less than three minutes.

2442
02:15:42,760 --> 02:15:44,262
Come on, Watts. Come on, come on.

2443
02:15:44,345 --> 02:15:46,556
Blow the bomb, Harry. We're with you.

2444
02:15:46,639 --> 02:15:50,310
- Uh, it's stuck. Yes?
- You don't know the components!

2445
02:15:50,393 --> 02:15:53,896
Components, American components,
Russian components.

2446
02:15:53,980 --> 02:15:55,523
All made in Taiwan!

2447
02:15:55,857 --> 02:15:58,276
We're gettin' tight for ignition, <i>Freedom.</i>

2448
02:16:01,029 --> 02:16:02,405
Houston, we've got no fire.

2449
02:16:02,488 --> 02:16:04,574
- What does that mean?
- It means we got a busted ship.

2450
02:16:04,657 --> 02:16:07,243
A busted ship?
And I'm strapped in here.

2451
02:16:07,327 --> 02:16:09,245
I had a great spot picked out there.

2452
02:16:09,620 --> 02:16:10,747
<i>Freedom,</i> you fire that engine.

2453
02:16:10,830 --> 02:16:12,915
If there's not a way, you find a way.
The clock's tickin'.

2454
02:16:12,999 --> 02:16:14,876
<i>Let's go!</i>
<i>Let's fire that engine,</i> Freedom!

2455
02:16:15,585 --> 02:16:18,755
You got less than a minute.
Don't think I won't blow this thing.

2456
02:16:20,673 --> 02:16:23,176
Sharp, get out of here.
It's gettin' bad down here.

2457
02:16:23,259 --> 02:16:25,345
I know how to fix it. Please, move.

2458
02:16:25,428 --> 02:16:27,764
I... I have to take you away
if you don't move.

2459
02:16:27,847 --> 02:16:30,850
Watts, you gotta get that shuttle started.
You gotta fire it up now!

2460
02:16:30,933 --> 02:16:32,894
Damn it, Sharp. Get off this rock!

2461
02:16:32,977 --> 02:16:35,063
I'm telling you, please, move!

2462
02:16:35,146 --> 02:16:40,360
This is how we fix problem
in the Russian space station.

2463
02:16:40,443 --> 02:16:43,529
Because I don't want
to stay here any more.

2464
02:16:43,613 --> 02:16:45,281
[ Whirring ]

2465
02:16:45,365 --> 02:16:49,243
Yeah! Finally! We can go home!

2466
02:16:49,327 --> 02:16:51,662
- She's coming back. She's coming back.
- We're hot!

2467
02:16:51,746 --> 02:16:54,290
Watts! Let's go, let's go!

2468
02:16:54,749 --> 02:16:57,460
Rain all you want, you son of a bitch.

2469
02:16:58,169 --> 02:17:01,214
Let's go! We don't have time!
Hurry, hurry. We got no time!

2470
02:17:01,297 --> 02:17:03,257
Initiate thrusters on my mark!

2471
02:17:03,341 --> 02:17:05,218
Two, one, mark!

2472
02:17:13,267 --> 02:17:15,103
Come on. Get some altitude.
Let's go, let's go.

2473
02:17:15,978 --> 02:17:17,605
[ Yelling ]

2474
02:17:18,439 --> 02:17:20,525
<i>Freedom</i> has max thrust!

2475
02:17:27,323 --> 02:17:29,117
Thank you, Harry.

2476
02:17:35,998 --> 02:17:37,542
[ Screaming ]

2477
02:17:40,128 --> 02:17:41,921
Shuttle's out of range.
Still no detonation.

2478
02:17:42,004 --> 02:17:43,756
[ Grunting ]

2479
02:17:46,759 --> 02:17:49,095
Something's not right.
Too much time has gone by.

2480
02:17:51,347 --> 02:17:53,599
Zero barrier's about to be breached.
One minute.

2481
02:17:53,683 --> 02:17:56,436
Harry, come on. Press that button.

2482
02:17:56,519 --> 02:18:00,731
- We're goin' back and do it ourselves.
- Just don't. Wait one minute.

2483
02:18:00,815 --> 02:18:02,233
[ Grunting ]

2484
02:18:04,944 --> 02:18:06,529
Dan, we're about to cross the threshold.

2485
02:18:06,612 --> 02:18:07,905
Come on. Press the button.

2486
02:18:07,989 --> 02:18:12,869
Colonel, I'm askin' you.
Just one more minute!

2487
02:18:15,913 --> 02:18:17,457
[ Grunting ]

2488
02:18:19,625 --> 02:18:21,419
<i>Press the button, Stamper.</i>

2489
02:18:24,589 --> 02:18:25,882
Come on.

2490
02:18:28,718 --> 02:18:31,012
Harry'll do it. I know it.

2491
02:18:32,388 --> 02:18:33,890
He doesn't know how to fail.

2492
02:18:41,772 --> 02:18:43,566
We win, Gracie!

2493
02:18:44,609 --> 02:18:45,693
Press it!

2494
02:18:45,776 --> 02:18:46,903
[ Beeping ]

2495
02:19:16,891 --> 02:19:18,434
[ Screaming ]

2496
02:19:18,935 --> 02:19:22,021
<i>[ Man On P.A. I We have detonation.
Confirming detonation.</i>

2497
02:19:39,539 --> 02:19:41,874
<i>The two halves are gonna miss us
by 400 miles,</i>

2498
02:19:41,958 --> 02:19:44,877
<i>and most of the small particles
have been vaporized.</i>

2499
02:19:56,305 --> 02:19:59,058
- Houston, we're comin' home.
<i>- We copy that,</i> Freedom.

2500
02:19:59,141 --> 02:20:02,478
Yo, Harry, you the man.

2501
02:20:55,781 --> 02:20:59,619
Kennedy, we see you.
And you never looked so good.

2502
02:20:59,702 --> 02:21:03,331
I never told anybody this before
but I hate flyin',

2503
02:21:03,414 --> 02:21:05,333
so it'd be an awful shame to die now.

2504
02:21:05,416 --> 02:21:09,670
That's easy for you to say. I owe
100 grand to a bad-ass loan shark,

2505
02:21:09,754 --> 02:21:12,381
which I spent on a stripper
named Molly Mounds.

2506
02:21:12,506 --> 02:21:14,050
Boy, that's bad.

2507
02:21:14,133 --> 02:21:17,762
Kennedy, we are 100 percent.
Flap suspension control on full.

2508
02:21:30,775 --> 02:21:32,735
<i>[ Man ] Welcome home, astronauts.</i>

2509
02:21:41,160 --> 02:21:43,454
Hey, guys, remember,
we're heroes now.

2510
02:21:43,537 --> 02:21:45,915
So that incident with me
and the gun on the asteroid,

2511
02:21:45,998 --> 02:21:48,459
let's keep that under wraps, all right?

2512
02:22:52,690 --> 02:22:54,442
Miss Stamper.

2513
02:22:56,068 --> 02:22:58,821
Colonel Willie Sharp,
United States Air Force, ma'am.

2514
02:22:59,488 --> 02:23:02,450
Requesting permission to shake
the hand of the daughter

2515
02:23:02,533 --> 02:23:04,994
of the bravest man I've ever met.

2516
02:23:11,500 --> 02:23:12,918
Hello. [ Speaking French ]

2517
02:23:13,002 --> 02:23:15,755
- Oh, my God!
- Hi, you're my hero.

2518
02:23:15,838 --> 02:23:18,549
Oh, baby, I wanna have babies with you.

2519
02:23:21,677 --> 02:23:23,637
Welcome back, cowboy.

2520
02:23:25,181 --> 02:23:29,435
Uh, Harry wanted you to have this.

2521
02:23:35,900 --> 02:23:37,610
He did, huh?

2522
02:23:56,128 --> 02:23:57,713
<i>I could stay awake</i>

2523
02:23:57,797 --> 02:24:01,550
<i>Just to hear you breathin'</i>

2524
02:24:03,052 --> 02:24:06,555
<i>Watch you smile while you are sleepin'</i>

2525
02:24:07,056 --> 02:24:10,851
<i>While you're far away and dreamin'</i>

2526
02:24:11,644 --> 02:24:15,189
<i>I just wanna stay with you</i>

2527
02:24:15,272 --> 02:24:18,442
<i>In this moment forever</i>

2528
02:24:18,526 --> 02:24:21,237
<i>Forever and ever</i>

2529
02:24:21,320 --> 02:24:25,324
<i>I don't wanna close my eyes</i>

2530
02:24:25,407 --> 02:24:27,827
<i>I don't wanna fall asleep</i>

2531
02:24:27,910 --> 02:24:30,037
<i>'Cause I miss you, baby</i>

2532
02:24:30,120 --> 02:24:32,957
<i>And I don't wanna miss a thing</i>

2533
02:24:33,207 --> 02:24:36,752
<i>'Cause even when I dream of you</i>

2534
02:24:37,336 --> 02:24:39,839
<i>The sweetest dream would never do</i>

2535
02:24:39,922 --> 02:24:41,924
<i>I'd still miss you, baby</i>

2536
02:24:42,007 --> 02:24:45,177
<i>And I don't wanna miss a thing</i>

2537
02:24:45,261 --> 02:24:49,181
<i>And I don't wanna miss one smile</i>

2538
02:24:49,265 --> 02:24:52,601
<i>And I don't wanna miss one kiss</i>

2539
02:24:53,227 --> 02:24:56,772
<i>Well, I just wanna be
with you right here</i>

2540
02:24:56,856 --> 02:25:00,609
<i>With you just like this</i>

2541
02:25:01,026 --> 02:25:04,905
<i>Well, I just wanna hold you close</i>

2542
02:25:05,114 --> 02:25:09,034
<i>Feel your heart so close to mine</i>

2543
02:25:09,577 --> 02:25:13,080
<i>And just stay here in this moment</i>

2544
02:25:13,163 --> 02:25:17,835
<i>For all the rest of time</i>

2545
02:25:18,085 --> 02:25:20,170
<i>Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah</i>

2546
02:25:20,254 --> 02:25:23,048
<i>Yeah</i>

2547
02:25:23,215 --> 02:25:26,343
<i>Don't wanna close my eyes</i>

2548
02:25:26,969 --> 02:25:29,430
<i>I don't wanna fall asleep</i>

2549
02:25:29,513 --> 02:25:31,515
<i>'Cause I miss you, baby</i>

2550
02:25:31,599 --> 02:25:34,685
<i>And I don't wanna miss a thing</i>

2551
02:25:34,810 --> 02:25:38,355
<i>'Cause even when I dream of you</i>

2552
02:25:38,814 --> 02:25:41,275
<i>The sweetest dream would never do</i>

2553
02:25:41,358 --> 02:25:43,402
<i>I'd still miss you, baby</i>

2554
02:25:43,485 --> 02:25:46,405
<i>And I don't wanna miss a thing</i>

2555
02:25:46,947 --> 02:25:49,658
<i>Don't wanna close my eyes</i>

2556
02:25:50,117 --> 02:25:54,371
<i>I don't wanna fall asleep</i>

2557
02:25:54,455 --> 02:25:58,125
<i>Yeah
I don't wanna miss a thing</i>

2558
02:28:55,636 --> 02:28:58,013
<i>[ Woman Vocalizing]</i>

2559
02:29:03,602 --> 02:29:08,023
<i>All my bags are packed
I'm ready to go</i>

2560
02:29:08,357 --> 02:29:11,735
<i>I'm standin' here outside your door</i>

2561
02:29:12,194 --> 02:29:17,324
<i>I hate to wake you up to say goodbye</i>

2562
